 the full picture of RVC Next: package structure and layer rules, service assembly, process responsibilities, a request's round trip from browser to engine, and shared infrastructure for errors, settings, events, the database and data directory. Each layer is covered in detail in Engine, Core services, API and events, Web UI and CLI implementation.","locale":"en"},"8115":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-14","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`tests/test_architecture.py` uses `ast` to inspect each module's `import` statements (absolute imports only) against the table below; the standard library is always allowed.","locale":"en"},"8116":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-15","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"Layer","locale":"en"},"8117":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-16","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"Allowed `rvc_next` subpackages","locale":"en"},"8118":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-17","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"Allowed third-party modules","locale":"en"},"8119":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-18","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`engine`","locale":"en"},"8120":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-19","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`engine`","locale":"en"},"8121":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-20","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"numpy, scipy, torch, transformers, faiss, parselmouth, librosa, av, soundfile, onnxruntime, torch_directml, tensorboard, plus `sounddevice` (only under `engine/audio_io/`), `pymss` and `pymss_core` (only under `engine/separate/`), `yaml`","locale":"en"},"8122":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-21","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`protocol`","locale":"en"},"8123":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-22","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`protocol`","locale":"en"},"8124":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-23","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"None","locale":"en"},"8125":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-24","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`workers`","locale":"en"},"8126":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-25","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`engine`, `protocol`, `workers`","locale":"en"},"8127":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-26","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"Same as engine, plus `sounddevice`, `pymss`, `yaml`","locale":"en"},"8128":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-27","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`core`","locale":"en"},"8129":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-28","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`core`, `engine`, `protocol`, `version`, `logger`","locale":"en"},"8130":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-29","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"pydantic, httpx, tomli, tomli_w, send2trash, numpy, typing_extensions","locale":"en"},"8131":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-30","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`api`","locale":"en"},"8132":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-31","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`api`, `core`, `version`, `logger`, `webui`","locale":"en"},"8133":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-32","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"fastapi, starlette, socketio, uvicorn, pydantic, anyio","locale":"en"},"8134":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-33","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`cli`","locale":"en"},"8135":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-34","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`cli`, `core`, `version`, `logger`, `api`","locale":"en"},"8136":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-35","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"typer, click, rich, pydantic, uvicorn","locale":"en"},"8137":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-36","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"Two additional subprocess tests check that importing `rvc_next.core.context` does not load `torch`, and that importing `rvc_next.cli.app` loads neither `torch` nor `fastapi`.","locale":"en"},"8138":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-37","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"Each rule has a purpose:","locale":"en"},"8139":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-38","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"**The engine knows nothing about the application.** It imports neither core, any Web / CLI framework, nor pydantic; parameters are frozen dataclasses (`VoiceParams`, `StreamParams`). Worker subprocesses and tests can therefore drive the engine directly, while core's `Record` models are the sole API shape. One problem in the original was that the engine returned Gradio update dictionaries and Chinese status text, making it unusable outside the UI.","locale":"en"},"8140":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-39","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"**Core imports no frameworks and never imports torch directly.** All 51 of its engine imports are inside functions. Commands such as `rvc-next version`, `config` and `--help` therefore avoid the cost of loading torch; the second test protects this.","locale":"en"},"8141":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-40","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"**`sounddevice` and `pymss` are confined to their own directories**, keeping changes to device access and the separation library local.","locale":"en"},"8142":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-41","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"**`protocol` uses only the standard library**, because both sides share it: the server and worker subprocesses must be able to import it without pulling in each other's dependencies.","locale":"en"},"8143":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-42","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"**`api` and `cli` never import `engine`.** The only import across interfaces is the `webui` command in `cli` importing `rvc_next.api.app.create_app` inside its function to start the server; the rule table allows `cli → api` and `uvicorn` for this.","locale":"en"},"8144":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-43","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#one-operation-one-core-method","content":"Each operation has exactly one core method, accepting and returning `Record` models (`core/record.py`). Routes and commands do only three things: parse input, call that method and shape the output. For conversion, the route body in `api/routers/convert.py` only checks access to server paths, rejects CLI-only fields, then calls `return services.conversion.convert(body)`; the CLI's `convert` command constructs the same `ConvertRequest` and calls the same method (`foreground=True`).","locale":"en"},"8145":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-44","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#one-operation-one-core-method","content":"The API's JSON and CLI's `--json` output therefore have exactly the same shape: `test_model_json_matches_api_shape` in `tests/cli/test_cli.py` directly compares `rvc-next model list --json` with `GET /api/v1/models`. `Record` sets `json_schema_serialization_defaults_required`, marking defaulted fields as required in the output schema, so the generated TypeScript types match what the server actually sends.","locale":"en"},"8146":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-45","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"`build_services()` in `core/context.py` constructs all services once in dependency order and returns a `Services` dataclass:","locale":"en"},"8147":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-46","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"8148":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-47","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"Class","locale":"en"},"8149":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-48","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"Responsibility","locale":"en"},"8150":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-49","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"`settings`","locale":"en"},"8151":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-50","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"`SettingsService`","locale":"en"},"8152":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-51","page_id":"/en/docs/de