,"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"Avoid audio glitches; callbacks must not block","locale":"en"},"9617":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-94","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"Change block length without stopping the stream to reload","locale":"en"},"9618":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-95","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"Block, crossfade, or context changes require stopping the stream","locale":"en"},"9619":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-96","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"Rebuild buffers, keep the voice loaded","locale":"en"},"9620":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-97","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"—","locale":"en"},"9621":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-98","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"Resume training","locale":"en"},"9622":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-99","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"Repeats the saved epoch after restoration","locale":"en"},"9623":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-100","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"Continues from the next epoch","locale":"en"},"9624":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-101","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"—","locale":"en"},"9625":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-102","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"mp3/m4a output","locale":"en"},"9626":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-103","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"`wav2` leaves sample rate unchanged; 40k models fail to export mp3/m4a","locale":"en"},"9627":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-104","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"Raise to the nearest encoder-supported rate (40 kHz → 44.1 kHz)","locale":"en"},"9628":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-105","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"—","locale":"en"},"9629":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-106","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"Other differences visible during comparison, without being behavior changes:","locale":"en"},"9630":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-107","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"**Offline output is up to two 10 ms frames shorter**—the original's per-chunk flooring; preserved for bit-identical results.","locale":"en"},"9631":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-108","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"**transformers 5**: the original pins below 4.50; rvc-next needs `transformers>=5,<6` (4.x requires `huggingface_hub < 1`). HuBERT layer outputs are unchanged and golden runs are bit-identical.","locale":"en"},"9632":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-109","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"**Index k-means** uses faiss rather than scikit-learn MiniBatchKMeans (only above 200,000 vectors), removing a dependency; same purpose, different numbers.","locale":"en"},"9633":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-110","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#intentional-behavior-changes","content":"**CUDA Graph switches**: the original uses `RVC_CUDA_GRAPH`; rvc-next uses settings `compute.cuda_graph_offline` (default off) and `compute.cuda_graph_live` (default on); the cache capacity variable is renamed to `RVC_NEXT_CUDA_GRAPH_MAX_CACHE`. Golden code clears `RVC_CUDA_GRAPH` before running.","locale":"en"},"9634":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-111","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#porting-torchaudio-and-torchfcpe","content":"The original uses torchaudio for live resampling and torchfcpe for FCPE. torchaudio's last version is 2.11, and it declares no torch dependency, so unconstrained torch can resolve to a version it cannot load; torchfcpe also pulls in torchaudio. rvc-next therefore ports the parts it uses and no longer depends on either package:","locale":"en"},"9635":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-112","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#porting-torchaudio-and-torchfcpe","content":"Port","locale":"en"},"9636":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-113","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#porting-torchaudio-and-torchfcpe","content":"Source","locale":"en"},"9637":{"id":"/en/docs/development-parity-114","page_id":"/en/docs/development-parity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-parity#porting-torchaudio-and-torchfcpe","co