ets","content":"Real assets","locale":"en"},"9745":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-4","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-setup#scriptsdevpy","content":"`scripts/dev.py`","locale":"en"},"9746":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-5","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-setup#dev-run-api-and-vite-together","content":"`dev`: run API and Vite together","locale":"en"},"9747":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-6","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-setup#building-the-wheel","content":"Building the wheel","locale":"en"},"9748":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-7","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-setup#publishing","content":"Publishing","locale":"en"},"9749":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-8","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-setup#building-the-documentation-site","content":"Building the documentation site","locale":"en"},"9750":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-9","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-setup#dependency-constraints","content":"Dependency constraints","locale":"en"},"9751":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-10","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-setup#code-conventions-at-a-glance","content":"Code conventions at a glance","locale":"en"},"9752":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-11","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-setup#git-workflow","content":"Git workflow","locale":"en"},"9753":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-12","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"RVC Next **runs only in its own environment**: an isolated venv or a separate Python installation, never shared with other projects. Dependency constraints require this (see “Dependency constraints” below): `transformers` 5.x requires `huggingface_hub < 2` through `tokenizers`, so it cannot coexist with projects using `huggingface_hub` 2.x; pymss and torchaudio release schedules also confine `torch` to a version window.","locale":"en"},"9754":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-13","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"The development environment is `.venv` at the repository root (listed in `.gitignore`), created with uv from a Python 3.11 interpreter, without inheriting system site-packages:","locale":"en"},"9755":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-14","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"From then on, run everything with `.venv/bin/python` (or `python` after activation), including `python scripts/dev.py ...`: `dev.py` uses **the interpreter running it** (`sys.executable`), rather than the first `python` on `PATH`.","locale":"en"},"9756":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-15","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"Install torch first for the same reason as in a user installation: `pyproject.toml` declares only `torch>=2.7.1`, without specifying a build variant. Install the build for your hardware from the PyTorch index first; the subsequent `pip install` sees that the constraint is satisfied and will not fetch another build from PyPI (usually a large CUDA package).","locale":"en"},"9757":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-16","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"RVC Next has ported torchaudio's `Resample` and torchfcpe's FCPE inference path and no longer imports either package itself (the layer tests enforce this). Only two kinds of tests use them, and skip automatically when they are absent:","locale":"en"},"9758":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-17","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"Cases in `tests/engine/test_sinc_resample.py` and `tests/engine/test_fcpe_model.py` that compare results bit for bit with the original libraries;","locale":"en"},"9759":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-18","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"Code on **the original's side** of the golden tests (the original's live code imports torchaudio, and its FCPE imports torchfcpe).","locale":"en"},"9760":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-19","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"To run these cases, install torchaudio and torch **as a matching pair** at the same version: torchaudio's final release is 2.11, it declares no torch requirement, and it refuses to load alongside newer torch versions.","locale":"en"},"9761":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-20","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"Other opt-in dependencies are also declared in `pyproject.toml`:","locale":"en"},"9762":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-21","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"TensorBoard training logs: `uv pip install -e '.[tensorboard]'`.","locale":"en"},"9763":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-22","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"Comparisons against the original libraries: install matching torch / torchaudio builds as described above, then run `uv pip install --group parity`; this group also contains the torchcrepe, torchfcpe and SwiftF0 reference implementations and is separate from `dev`.","locale":"en"},"9764":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-23","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#isolated-virtual-environment","content":"Extracting SwiftF0 weights again: `uv pip install --group extract-swift-f0`, then run `scripts/extract_swift_f0.py`.","locale":"en"},"9765":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-24","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#other-system-dependencies","content":"Dependency","locale":"en"},"9766":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-25","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#other-system-dependencies","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"9767":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-26","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#other-system-dependencies","content":"Installation","locale":"en"},"9768":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-27","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#other-system-dependencies","content":"PortAudio (`libportaudio2` on Linux)","locale":"en"},"9769":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-28","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#other-system-dependencies","content":"`sounddevice` opens audio devices; live voice conversion and device enumeration tests need it","locale":"en"},"9770":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-29","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#other-system-dependencies","content":"System package manager; CI uses `sudo apt-get install -y libportaudio2`","locale":"en"}