"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"`@material/web` is in maintenance mode; a wrapper makes individual replacements easier","locale":"en"},"10065":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-39","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"Color","locale":"en"},"10066":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-40","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"`@material/material-color-utilities` 0.4","locale":"en"},"10067":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-41","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"Generates all MD3 color roles from one source color","locale":"en"},"10068":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-42","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"Font","locale":"en"},"10069":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-43","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"`@fontsource-variable/roboto-flex`","locale":"en"},"10070":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-44","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"Bundled for offline use","locale":"en"},"10071":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-45","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"Testing","locale":"en"},"10072":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-46","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"vitest 5 + happy-dom, `@vue/test-utils`","locale":"en"},"10073":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-47","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"Package manager","locale":"en"},"10074":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-48","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"bun (`bun.lock`)","locale":"en"},"10075":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-49","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"`scripts/dev.py` checks `PATH` first, then `~/.bun/bin`","locale":"en"},"10076":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-50","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"Charts and waveforms use no third-party libraries: server-computed peaks are drawn on canvas (`ui/Waveform.vue`), loss curves use `ui/LineChart.vue`, and level meters and progress bars use ordinary elements with CSS transforms.","locale":"en"},"10077":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-51","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#technology-stack","content":"Scripts in `package.json`: `dev` (Vite), `build` (`vue-tsc --noEmit` then `vite build`), `build:only`, `typecheck`, `test` (`vitest run`). For daily use, call them through `scripts/dev.py`: `web-install`, `web`, `web-dev`, `test-web` (tests + type checking), `dev` (API and Vite together, with Vite hot module replacement); see Development environment.","locale":"en"},"10078":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-52","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#development-proxy","content":"`vite.config.ts` proxies `/api`, `/openapi.json`, and `/ws` (WebSocket) to `RVC_NEXT_BACKEND` (default `http://127.0.0.1:7868`), so the browser sees only Vite's origin and needs no CORS. During development, the API process is often restarted after Python changes (it does not reload automatically; restart it manually), and the socket reconnects every few seconds. For backend-unavailable errors such as `ECONNREFUSED` and `ECONNRESET`, the proxy prints one throttled message (at most every 5 seconds) and returns 502 JSON (`code: \"api_unreachable\"`) for HTTP requests instead of leaving the browser waiting. Other errors are printed in full as usual. `isExpectedProxyError` is tested by `devProxy.test.ts`.","locale":"en"},"10079":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-53","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#development-proxy","content":"`vite.config.ts` also declares tags starting with `md-` as custom elements, maps the `@` alias to `src/`, and inlines `@material/material-color-utilities` in tests (version 0.4.0 has an extensionless import that plain Node cannot resolve).","locale":"en"},"10080":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-54","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"Route","locale":"en"},"10081":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-55","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"View","locale":"en"},"10082":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-56","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`meta.screen`","locale":"en"},"10083":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-57","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`/convert`","locale":"en"},"10084":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-58","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`ConvertView`","locale":"en"},"10085":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-59","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`convert`","locale":"en"},"10086":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-60","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`/live`","locale":"en"},"10087":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-61","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`LiveView`","locale":"en"},"10088":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-62","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`live`","locale":"en"},"10089":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-63","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`/separate`","locale":"en"},"10090":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-64","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`SeparateView`","locale":"en"},"10091":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-65","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`separate`","locale":"en"},"10092":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-66","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`/train`, `/train/:name`","locale":"en"},"10093":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-67","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`TrainView`, `ExperimentView`","locale":"en"},"10094":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-68","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`train`","locale":"en"},"10095":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-69","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`/models`, `/models/:id`","locale":"en"},"10096":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-70","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`ModelsView` (five tabs: Voices, Base models, Separation models, Assets, Tools), `ModelDetailView`","locale":"en"},"10097":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-71","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`models`","locale":"en"},"10098":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-72","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`/jobs`","locale":"en"},"10099":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-73","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`JobsView`","locale":"en"},"10100":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-74","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`jobs`","locale":"en"},"10101":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-75","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`/settings`","locale":"en"},"10102":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-76","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`SettingsView` (General, Compute, Audio, Storage, Downloads, Training defaults, Appearance, About)","locale":"en"},"10103":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-77","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`settings`","locale":"en"},"10104":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-78","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`/dev`","locale":"en"},"10105":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-79","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`DevComponentsView` (a showcase of all shared components for checking theme and motion)","locale":"en"},"10106":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-80","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`dev`","locale":"en"},"10107":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-81","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#directory-structure","content":"`/` redirects to the last destination (`Preferences.lastScreen`, read directly from localStorage because Pinia is not ready yet); unknown paths redirect to `/convert`. `router.ts` also remembers each destination's last full address (`addressOf`), so navigation returns to the experiment or voice left open instead of its list; this record stays in memory.","locale":"en"},"10108":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-82","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#ui-the-design-system-layer","content":"`src/ui/` is the only place that imports `@material/web` and `@lucide/vue` (with additional test patches in `test/setup.ts`); views and feature components import only from `@/ui` (`ui/index.ts`). This layer isolates risk: `@material/web` no longer adds components, so if one fails in a browser, it can be replaced in `ui/` without changing application code. Icons are re-exported through `ui/icons.ts` and rendered with `<AppIcon :icon=\"icons.X\" />`.","locale":"en"},"10109":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-83","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#ui-the-design-system-layer","content":"There are two kinds of components:","locale":"en"},"10110":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-84","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#ui-the-design-system-layer","content":"**Wrappers around `md-*` elements**: `AppButton`, `IconButton`, `Fab`, `Checkbox`, `Switch`, `Slider`, `TextField`, `Tabs`, `SegmentedButton` (also exported as `SegmentedControl`), `FilterChip`, `Divider`, `ProgressCircle`, `ProgressBar` (only its indeterminate form), `ParamSlider`. They define props, event names, and types, without layering extra animation over the built-in `md-*` animation.","locale":"en"},"10111":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-85","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#ui-the-design-system-layer","content":"**Custom components** (missing from or unsuitable in `@material/web`): `AppShell`, `NavigationRail`, `NavigationBar`, `TopAppBar`, `AppCard`, `Surface`, `AppDialog`, `ConfirmDialog`, `SideSheet`, `Snackbar`, `Tooltip`, `AppMenu`, `ContextMenu`, `SelectField`, `DeviceMenu`, `SearchField`, `TokenField`, `PathField`, `DataList`, `Breadcrumbs`, `Stepper`, `ExpansionPanel`, `EmptyState`, `Skeleton`, `Badge`, `Chip`, `KeyHint`, `DropZone`, `Waveform`, `LineChart`, `LevelMeter`, `PageFooter`.","locale":"en"},"10112":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-86","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#ui-the-design-system-layer","content":"Several mechanisms span components:","locale":"en"},"10113":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-87","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#ui-the-design-system-layer","content":"`layers.ts` (`useLayer`, `useLayerBase`): the one record of what is open over the page — dialogs, side sheets, menus, an open picker or select — in opening order. A layer opened later paints above every earlier one (each kind keeps a floor in `LAYER_Z`); `Escape` and a click outside close only the top layer; a modal layer makes the page and the layers under it `inert`; focus moves into a layer and back to whatever opened it.","locale":"en"},"10114":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-88","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#ui-the-design-system-layer","content":"`reveal.ts` (`revealDropdown`, `useRevealWhileOpen`): if an inline dropdown (voice picker, device menu) is hidden by the sticky `PageFooter`, scroll the container upward until it is visible, without passing the list's top. `PageFooter` marks itself with `data-page-footer`.","locale":"en"},"10115":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-89","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#ui-the-design-system-layer","content":"`useSnackbar`: a global queue, showing one message at a time.","locale":"en"},"10116":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-90","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#theme-and-tokens","content":"`theme/scheme.ts`: `DEFAULT_SOURCE_COLOR = '#3f5f90'` is the project's only hand-picked color (the logo blue); the color picker in Settings (`<input type=\"color\">`, as Hanaikada's) replaces it with any color. `generateScheme()` uses `SchemeTonalSpot` to generate every role in `ROLES`, supporting light/dark and contrast values 0, 0.5, and 1.","locale":"en"},"10117":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-91","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#theme-and-tokens","content":"`theme/applyTheme.ts` writes roles to `--md-sys-color-*` on `:root`; `watchSystemTheme` reacts to system changes in “System” mode. The inline script in `index.html` sets `data-theme` before the bundle loads to avoid an initial flash.","locale":"en"},"10118":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-92","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#theme-and-tokens","content":"`theme/tokens.css`: MD3 tokens for fonts, shapes, heights, motion, state layers (hover 8%, focus 12%, pressed 12%, dragged 16%), and project `--app-*` tokens: spacing `--app-space-*`, widths `--app-width-*` (all `clamp()`, growing with wider screens), in-page stacking `--app-z-*` (what opens over the page is stacked by `ui/layers.ts`), disabled opacity, etc.","locale":"en"},"10119":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-93","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#theme-and-tokens","content":"`theme/breakpoints.ts`: MD3 window size classes (600, 840, 1200, 1600 px). `AppShell` uses bottom navigation in compact mode (\\< 600 px), otherwise a navigation rail.","locale":"en"},"10120":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-94","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#theme-and-tokens","content":"Rules: components and views use tokens rather than literal colors, corner radii, font sizes, or durations (colors are enforced by `tokens.test.ts`); pair color roles (`on-primary` on `primary`); express hierarchy through surface tones first, shadows second.","locale":"en"},"10121":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-95","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Motion follows MD3's four patterns. Named transitions are centralized in `ui/motion/motion.css` and `TRANSITIONS` in `ui/motion/transitions.ts`; views use `<Transition :name=\"TRANSITIONS.x\">` instead of defining their own transitions. The principle is that every visible change is animated, with faster exits using an acceleration curve.","locale":"en"},"10122":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-96","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Name","locale":"en"},"10123":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-97","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"10124":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-98","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Actual use","locale":"en"},"10125":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-99","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`fade-through`","locale":"en"},"10126":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-100","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Switching between unrelated states","locale":"en"},"10127":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-101","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Destination-switching fallback without View Transitions","locale":"en"},"10128":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-102","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`shared-axis-x`","locale":"en"},"10129":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-103","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Peer tabs or steps; direction set by `--axis-dir`","locale":"en"},"10130":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-104","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Models tabs, Settings sections, the experiment's four steps; `useAxisDirection()` computes direction synchronously when the value changes","locale":"en"},"10131":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-105","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`container`","locale":"en"},"10132":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-106","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"A card grows into a dialog","locale":"en"},"10133":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-107","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`AppDialog` and `ModelDetailView` compute the initial transform with `containerFrom(from, to)`; without a source rectangle, fall back to a scaled fade-in","locale":"en"},"10134":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-108","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`sheet` / `scrim`","locale":"en"},"10135":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-109","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"A side sheet slides in from an edge","locale":"en"},"10136":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-110","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`SideSheet` (Jobs sheet)","locale":"en"},"10137":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-111","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`list`","locale":"en"},"10138":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-112","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Adding, removing, and reordering items (`TransitionGroup`)","locale":"en"},"10139":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-113","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Results, job cards, voice grids; `staggerStyle(i)` offsets each item by 20 ms, up to 12 items","locale":"en"},"10140":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-114","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`collapse`","locale":"en"},"10141":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-115","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Expand/collapse, height set by `collapseHooks`","locale":"en"},"10142":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-116","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`ExpansionPanel`, `JobCard`","locale":"en"},"10143":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-117","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`snackbar`","locale":"en"},"10144":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-118","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"Bottom notification","locale":"en"},"10145":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-119","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"`Snackbar`","locale":"en"},"10146":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-120","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"**Destination changes use the View Transitions API.** When the browser supports `document.startViewTransition`, `installViewTransitions(router)` in `ui/motion/viewTransition.ts` wraps navigation across destinations (`to.name !== from.name`) in a view transition; navigation within a destination is not wrapped. Key points:","locale":"en"},"10147":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-121","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"The browser pauses rendering during the update callback, including `requestAnimationFrame`, so the callback must finish on Vue's `nextTick` (when the new view is in the DOM), never wait for a frame—an early frame-based wait froze navigation.","locale":"en"},"10148":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-122","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"When a new navigation interrupts an unfinished transition, finish the old one first; rejected Promises from skipped transitions are all caught.","locale":"en"},"10149":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-123","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"When supported, `App.vue` renders views directly without `<Transition>`; otherwise it falls back to `<Transition mode=\"out-in\">` with `fade-through`.","locale":"en"},"10150":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-124","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"**The shell stays still.** Only the scroller `main.content` has `view-transition-name: app-content`; `motion.css` disables animation on the root snapshot, so navigation, indicators, and the top bar update in place while only page content fades out and in. The rounded background `.frame` belongs to the shell, outside the snapshot. Previously, the entire document root participated, so the entering `scale(0.92)` scaled the rail and top bar too.","locale":"en"},"10151":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-125","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"**Reduced motion.** With system `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` or “Reduced” in Settings (`<html data-motion=\"reduced\">`): all transitions become 100 ms linear fades without translation or scaling; view transitions become 100 ms crossfades without scaling; ripples are hidden; CSS animations become instantaneous. Destination changes still use view transitions under reduced motion—a short crossfade rather than a hard cut, because accessibility concerns movement, and abrupt jumps can also be uncomfortable. `prefersReducedMotion()` checks both sources.","locale":"en"},"10152":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-126","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#motion","content":"**High-frequency values.** Determinate `ProgressBar` bars are drawn directly: `md-linear-progress` restarts a 250 ms ease-in-out on every update, making values that change several times per second (Live load, uploads, jobs) stutter; the custom bar catches up to new values with an ease-out curve. `LevelMeter` moves with `transform` (no layout on each update), following audio-meter ballistics: fast rise, slow fall, with the peak tick falling slowest; `useFalling()` tracks the previous direction of change. `LiveStatsBar` bars glide smoothly between 10 Hz statistics.","locale":"en"},"10153":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-127","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Shared components make every feature feel part of one application; use them as the review checklist for each screen (AGENTS.md §7).","locale":"en"},"10154":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-128","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Component","locale":"en"},"10155":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-129","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Contract","locale":"en"},"10156":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-130","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Used in","locale":"en"},"10157":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-131","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`VoicePicker`","locale":"en"},"10158":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-132","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"The single voice-selection entry point: search by name, show sample rate, version, and speakers, mark voices without indexes; multi-speaker voices include a speaker menu (`v-model:speaker`)","locale":"en"},"10159":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-133","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Convert, Live","locale":"en"},"10160":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-134","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`VoiceParamsPanel`","locale":"en"},"10161":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-135","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"The single parameter panel: identical labels, ranges, defaults, help, and order everywhere. Ranges come from `paramSpecs.ts` (server schema), order from `VOICE_FIELDS` in `paramFields.ts`; selecting a voice loads its default preset (preserving the speaker); unavailable controls explain why (index strength without an index, consonant protection without pitch guidance); dragging applies immediately in `live` mode","locale":"en"},"10162":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-136","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Convert, Live","locale":"en"},"10163":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-137","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`StreamParamsPanel`","locale":"en"},"10164":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-138","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Live buffering and denoising parameters, each showing its share of estimated latency (`latencyShare`)","locale":"en"},"10165":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-139","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Live","locale":"en"},"10166":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-140","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`AudioSourceInput`","locale":"en"},"10167":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-141","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"The single way to supply audio: drop files, select server files (`ServerPathDialog`, within `paths.browse_roots`), or select previous results (`OutputsPickerDialog`); `folders` allows a whole server folder as one input","locale":"en"},"10168":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-142","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Convert, Separate, voice detail try-out","locale":"en"},"10169":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-143","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`JobCard` + `JobsSheet`","locale":"en"},"10170":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-144","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"One card per long operation: title, steps, progress, cancel, retry, “Run anyway”, logs (`JobLogView`); downloads show “88 MB / 210 MB · 8.4 MB/s · 14 seconds left”. Cards appear in the originating screen's `PageFooter` and the Jobs sheet; the sheet lists this session's jobs first, then merges recent REST history","locale":"en"},"10171":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-145","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"All screens","locale":"en"},"10172":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-146","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`ResultsList` + `ABCompare`","locale":"en"},"10173":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-147","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"One results list: waveforms (server peaks), playback, A/B against the source, download, reveal in file manager (local only), “Use as input”, “Re-run with these settings”, “Convert this”; `groupBySource` groups separated stems under their inputs. One player for the whole page (`stores/player.ts` wraps `audio/player.ts`); A/B switches sources at the same position","locale":"en"},"10174":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-148","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Convert, Separate, voice detail try-out","locale":"en"},"10175":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-149","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`AssetGate`","locale":"en"},"10176":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-150","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Missing assets show “Needs RMVPE — Download (size)” where the action would be, instead of an error; installation restores the action and emits `ready`","locale":"en"},"10177":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-151","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Convert, Live, Separate, Train, voice details","locale":"en"},"10178":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-152","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`ErrorNotice`","locale":"en"},"10179":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-153","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"A translated title by error code, the original server message, and expandable “Details” (`errorView` in `errors.ts`); tracebacks only appear in job logs","locale":"en"},"10180":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-154","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"All screens","locale":"en"},"10181":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-155","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`DevicePanel`","locale":"en"},"10182":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-156","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Device selection: full physical device names, server hostname in the title, input meter, test tone, optional monitor output, drivers under “Advanced”, problems beside the affected device; options are built in unit-testable `devices.ts`","locale":"en"},"10183":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-157","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Live, Settings › Audio","locale":"en"},"10184":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-158","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`LiveStatsBar`","locale":"en"},"10185":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-159","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Input/output levels, load bar (inference time / block length; above 0.8, use warning color and suggest a longer block), latency, underrun and overrun counts","locale":"en"},"10186":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-160","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Live","locale":"en"},"10187":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-161","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"`ResourceRow`","locale":"en"},"10188":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-162","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"One row for all downloadable or installed models: name and details, status, download progress with speed and time remaining, and download, verify, open, delete","locale":"en"},"10189":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-163","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"Models › Assets, Base models, Separation models, demo voices","locale":"en"},"10190":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-164","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"A few more conventions:","locale":"en"},"10191":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-165","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"**Screen hand-offs** (“Use as input”, “Convert this”, “Try”, “Re-run with these settings”) go through `stores/handoff.ts`: the sender calls `sendInputs(screen, items)` / `sendVoice(id, params)`, and the receiving screen consumes them with `take…()` when opened. They are not passed through URLs, avoiding paths or parameters in the address bar.","locale":"en"},"10192":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-166","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"**Imports**: every drop zone on Models (Voices, Base models, Separation models) calls `components/useModelImport.ts`: create a session, upload each file with progress, read the plan; commit immediately if `plan.confident`, otherwise pass the plan to `ImportReviewDialog`, where each index lists only compatible candidate voices plus “Keep unassigned”. Unassigned indexes appear in `IndexInbox` on Voices.","locale":"en"},"10193":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-167","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#unified-experience-contract","content":"**Consistent terminology**: `i18n.test.ts` checks fixed terms (Voice and its Chinese equivalent, Index strength, Consonant protection, Loudness match), and ensures the original's inconsistent terms (retrieved feature ratio, loudness factor, `rms_mix_rate`) never appear in copy.","locale":"en"},"10194":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-168","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-flow","content":"**REST is the sole source of truth.** `api = createClient<paths>({ baseUrl: BASE_URL })` in `api/client.ts` has middleware that adds `Authorization: Bearer` when a token exists and sets `useAuthStore().needed` on 401, opening `AuthDialog`. `unwrap()` converts `openapi-fetch` results into data or `ApiError(status, code, message, detail)`; `ApiError.missingAssets` reads `detail.assets` from `asset_missing`. Uploads use `uploadRaw()` (`XMLHttpRequest`, with progress); `urls` builds media URLs, and `<audio>` authenticates through the `rvc_next_token` cookie.","locale":"en"},"10195":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-169","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-flow","content":"**Queries**: `api/queries/<resource>.ts` wraps `useQuery`/`useMutation`; all keys live in `keys.ts`, shared with socket handlers. Successful mutations invalidate affected keys; job-starting mutations write the returned `Job` to the jobs store and record the originating screen (`jobs.upsert(job, 'convert')`).","locale":"en"},"10196":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-170","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-flow","content":"**Socket** (`api/socket.ts`): connect once at `${BASE_PATH}/ws/socket.io`, supplying the token in the handshake `auth` callback. Events either write directly to the cache (`assets_changed`, `live_state`, `devices_changed`, `compute_changed` carry full snapshots) or batch invalidation through `createInvalidator()`—each key is invalidated at most once per 300 ms, so a burst of events triggers only one refetch. See the event table in API and events for each handler.","locale":"en"},"10197":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-171","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-flow","content":"**High-frequency data goes into stores**: `stores/jobs.ts` (jobs and progress), `stores/live.ts` (live state and 10 Hz statistics, `load` = p95 inference time / block length), `stores/train.ts` (up to 20000 metric points per experiment, populated by REST, appended by events, deduplicated by epoch/step).","locale":"en"},"10198":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-172","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-flow","content":"**Out-of-order protection**: socket events can race REST snapshots. `isNewer()` in `jobs.ts` orders lifecycle stages (queued/waiting \\< running \\< cancelling \\< finished), never letting jobs move backward; after completion, use `finished_at` to choose the newer snapshot, and during execution, progress within a step only increases. `onFinished` listeners therefore fire once per job.","locale":"en"},"10199":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-173","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-flow","content":"**Reconnection**: on `connect`, `resync()` refetches active jobs and live state; on `reconnect`, also invalidate voices, outputs, jobs, assets, experiments, GPU memory, and device lists. This recovers events missed while disconnected.","locale":"en"},"10200":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-174","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-flow","content":"**Cross-screen notifications**: when a job started on another screen finishes or fails, `App.vue` shows a snackbar; failures include “Open log”.","locale":"en"},"10201":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-175","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-flow","content":"**Preferences** (`stores/preferences.ts`): theme, source color, contrast, language (`auto` follows the system), motion, last screen, last Convert voice, last Separate preset. Stored in localStorage (`rvc-next:preferences`, read by `index.html` and routing before Pinia), and, after loading the server copy, written to `client-state/preferences` with a 500 ms debounce to follow the user across browsers. A `version` field and `merge()` migrate old data (version 2 resets the old stuck reduced-motion preference to follow the system).","locale":"en"},"10202":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-176","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-flow","content":"**Deployment root**: `deriveBaseUrl(import.meta.url, origin)` in `api/baseUrl.ts` takes the part of the running script URL before its last `/assets/` as the root, so no API address is compiled into the build; the dev server has no `/assets/`, so the root is the page origin and Vite proxies requests. Scripts from other origins fall back to the page origin.","locale":"en"},"10203":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-177","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#shell-view-state-and-layout","content":"**Views stay mounted.** `App.vue` caches views with `<KeepAlive :max=\"12\">`, keyed by destination name, or full path for experiment and voice details (one instance per experiment or voice). Tabs, filters, and forms survive navigating away and back.","locale":"en"},"10204":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-178","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#shell-view-state-and-layout","content":"**Scroll positions.** Every page shares the shell's scroller, so `App.vue` records the departing page's `scrollTop` in `beforeEach` and restores it before showing the new view—before the view transition's update callback finishes (`nextTick`), or at `<Transition @enter>` on the fallback path—without jumps. This stays in memory: refreshing resets all views; only preferences persist.","locale":"en"},"10205":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-179","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#shell-view-state-and-layout","content":"**One column of sections.** Convert, Separate, Live, voice details, and Models › Tools use vertically stacked sections (`Surface`). Sections widen with the page; internal controls wrap in grids such as `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(280px, 100%), 1fr))`, rather than putting sections side by side. Run buttons, jobs started on the screen, and errors sit in the sticky `PageFooter`, always visible regardless of page length. Pages have no `max-width` and fill the content area.","locale":"en"},"10206":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-180","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#shell-view-state-and-layout","content":"**Container queries.** `main.content` is the size container `app-content` (`container: app-content / inline-size`). Pages adapt to their actual width (currently, tighter padding at `@container app-content (max-width: 599px)`), rather than window width—rails and side sheets change the available space.","locale":"en"},"10207":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-181","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#shell-view-state-and-layout","content":"**Field rows**: rows with a button beside a field (Add, Browse, Build) use `align-items: center` to center the button against the field.","locale":"en"},"10208":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-182","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#shell-view-state-and-layout","content":"**Shrinkable names**: audio filenames and voice names are often long unbreakable strings; flex items default to `min-width: auto`, pushing buttons offscreen, so text elements must declare `min-width: 0` to allow ellipsis.","locale":"en"},"10209":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-183","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#shell-view-state-and-layout","content":"`src/layout.test.ts` checks these rules by reading styles from source files (with explicit file and selector lists). Add new name-bearing rows or section pages to the corresponding list.","locale":"en"},"10210":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-184","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#internationalization","content":"`src/i18n/index.ts` is a small implementation: nested message objects, `t(key, params)` (`{name}` placeholders), fallback to English, then to the key; `tOr(key, fallback)` handles keys built from server values (error codes, stage IDs), showing a readable fallback when no message exists. Languages are `en` and `zh-CN`; with `auto`, `detectLocale()` chooses by browser language (any `zh`/`zh-*` maps to `zh-CN`) and responds to `languagechange`.","locale":"en"},"10211":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-185","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#internationalization","content":"`i18n.test.ts` requires identical keys and placeholders in `zh-CN` and `en`, and checks fixed terminology. Device problem messages from the server are in English: the UI translates reason codes and displays server messages unchanged (AGENTS.md §7).","locale":"en"},"10212":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-186","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"`bun run test` (vitest, happy-dom) and `bun run typecheck` (`vue-tsc`) are run by `python scripts/dev.py test-web`, also part of `check`.","locale":"en"},"10213":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-187","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Type","locale":"en"},"10214":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-188","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Files","locale":"en"},"10215":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-189","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"What they enforce","locale":"en"},"10216":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-190","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Rule","locale":"en"},"10217":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-191","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"`imports.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"10218":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-192","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Modules within `src/` import each other only through `@/` aliases, without relative paths","locale":"en"},"10219":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-193","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Rule","locale":"en"},"10220":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-194","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"`tokens.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"10221":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-195","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"No hexadecimal colors in styles or templates outside `src/theme/`","locale":"en"},"10222":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-196","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Rule","locale":"en"},"10223":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-197","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"`layout.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"10224":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-198","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Shrinkable names, one column of sections + `PageFooter`, centered field rows, no grids placing sections side by side","locale":"en"},"10225":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-199","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Rule","locale":"en"},"10226":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-200","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"`i18n/i18n.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"10227":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-201","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Matching keys and placeholders in both languages; fixed terminology","locale":"en"},"10228":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-202","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Motion","locale":"en"},"10229":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-203","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"`ui/motion/motion.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"10230":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-204","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Exits finish under the zero-duration test stylesheet (`test/motion-zero.css`) with both full and reduced motion (no waiting forever for `transitionend` at duration 0); rules cover both reduced-motion sources; destination changes use view transitions; reduced motion uses a short crossfade","locale":"en"},"10231":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-205","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Component","locale":"en"},"10232":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-206","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"`ui/ui.test.ts`, `ui/layers.test.ts`, `ui/bars.test.ts`, `ui/reveal.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"10233":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-207","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Primitive behavior, layer stack, motion helpers, color generation, window size classes, formatting; progress bars and meters; dropdowns clear the footer","locale":"en"},"10234":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-208","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Feature","locale":"en"},"10235":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-209","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"`VoiceParamsPanel.test.ts`, `ImportReviewDialog.test.ts`, `ResourceRow.test.ts`, `GpuIndicator.test.ts`, `devices.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"10236":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-210","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Schema-derived parameter ranges, default presets and disabled reasons; compatible voices only; download rows; GPU memory release availability; device menu ordering and resolution states","locale":"en"},"10237":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-211","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"State","locale":"en"},"10238":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-212","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"`stores/jobs.test.ts`, `stores/preferences.test.ts`, `audio/player.test.ts`, `api/baseUrl.test.ts`, `devProxy.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"10239":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-213","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"Jobs never regress, completion is notified once; preference migration; A/B player; deployment root derivation; proxy error classification","locale":"en"},"10240":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-214","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#tests","content":"`test/setup.ts` patches `HTMLElement` with `attachInternals`: happy-dom lacks `ElementInternals`, but `@material/web` form-associated elements (buttons, fields) call it during creation. Component tests mount with `@vue/test-utils`, mocking queries and stores as needed.","locale":"en"},"10241":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-215","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#adding-a-screen","content":"**API first.** If new endpoints are needed, add them in the core and `api/routers/`, run `python scripts/dev.py typegen`, and alias frequently used schemas in `api/types.ts` (see API and events).","locale":"en"},"10242":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-216","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#adding-a-screen","content":"**Queries.** Add keys in `api/queries/keys.ts` and `useQuery`/`useMutation` in `api/queries/<resource>.ts`; job-starting mutations write `Job` to `useJobsStore().upsert(job, '<screen>')`.","locale":"en"},"10243":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-217","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#adding-a-screen","content":"**Events.** When new or existing events affect new data, write or invalidate the corresponding keys in `api/socket.ts`; put high-frequency data in stores, outside the cache.","locale":"en"},"10244":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-218","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#adding-a-screen","content":"**Views.** Create `XxxView.vue` in `views/`, add a route in `router.ts`, and set `meta.screen`. For a navigation destination, add an item to `nav` in `App.vue` (using `addressOf()`), and update `SCREENS` in `router.ts` and the list tracking `lastScreen` in `App.vue`.","locale":"en"},"10245":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-219","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#adding-a-screen","content":"**Composition.** Import primitives only from `@/ui`, favoring unified experience components; use `.sections` with one column of `Surface` sections, actions in `PageFooter`, and `min-width: 0` on text elements in name-bearing rows; add the new file to the corresponding lists in `layout.test.ts`. Use names from `TRANSITIONS`, without literal durations or colors. Add missing primitives to `ui/` and export them from `ui/index.ts`, rather than patching call sites.","locale":"en"},"10246":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-220","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#adding-a-screen","content":"**Copy.** Add keys to both `i18n/en.ts` and `i18n/zh-CN.ts`.","locale":"en"},"10247":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-221","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#adding-a-screen","content":"**Checks.** Run `python scripts/dev.py test-web`, then exercise the screen in a browser with `python scripts/dev.py dev`, including narrow screens (\\< 600 px) and reduced motion; new components can go in `DevComponentsView` to check theme and motion.","locale":"en"},"10248":{"id":"/en/docs/development","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"page","content":"Development documentation","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development","locale":"en"},"10249":{"id":"/en/docs/development-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development","content":"This section is for anyone modifying, extending or reviewing the RVC Next code: maintainers, contributors and coding agents working in this repository.","locale":"en"},"10250":{"id":"/en/docs/development-1","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development#relationship-to-agentsmd","content":"Relationship to AGENTS.md","locale":"en"},"10251":{"id":"/en/docs/development-2","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"Page map","locale":"en"},"10252":{"id":"/en/docs/development-3","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"Project origins","locale":"en"},"10253":{"id":"/en/docs/development-4","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development#licence","content":"Licence","locale":"en"},"10254":{"id":"/en/docs/development-5","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development","content":"This section is for anyone modifying, extending or reviewing the RVC Next code: maintainers, contributors and coding agents working in this repository. It explains how the code is built **today**, why each rule exists, and where it must stay consistent with the original RVC. For usage, see Quick start and the User guide; for individual commands, see Command line.","locale":"en"},"10255":{"id":"/en/docs/development-6","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#relationship-to-agentsmd","content":"`AGENTS.md` at the repository root (in English; `CLAUDE.md` only references it) is the **design record**: a concise account of what the code does, which rules it keeps, and where it departs from the original plan. It lives alongside the code and changes with it, and is the sole authoritative summary of how the code stands today.","locale":"en"},"10256":{"id":"/en/docs/development-7","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#relationship-to-agentsmd","content":"The responsibilities of these pages and that file are:","locale":"en"},"10257":{"id":"/en/docs/development-8","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#relationship-to-agentsmd","content":"`AGENTS.md`","locale":"en"},"10258":{"id":"/en/docs/development-9","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#relationship-to-agentsmd","content":"Development documentation (this section)","locale":"en"},"10259":{"id":"/en/docs/development-10","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#relationship-to-agentsmd","content":"Language","locale":"en"},"10260":{"id":"/en/docs/development-11","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#relationship-to-agentsmd","content":"English","locale":"en"},"10261":{"id":"/en/docs/development-12","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#relationship-to-agentsmd","content":"Simplified Chinese","locale":"en"},"10262":{"id":"/en/docs/development-13","page_id":"/en/docs/development","t