url":"/en/docs/guide-models","content":"Base models for training: official models and your imported G/D models","locale":"en"},"11142":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models","content":"**Separation models**","locale":"en"},"11143":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models","content":"Built-in and imported separation models","locale":"en"},"11144":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models","content":"**Assets**","locale":"en"},"11145":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models","content":"All downloadable files: HuBERT, the pitch models (RMVPE, FCPE, CREPE), base models, separation models and demo voices","locale":"en"},"11146":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models","content":"**Tools**","locale":"en"},"11147":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models","content":"Merge two voices; extract a voice from a training checkpoint","locale":"en"},"11148":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"The **Voices** tab lists all voices in the library as cards. Each card shows the name, sample rate · version · **pitch guidance**/**no pitch guidance**, and labels:","locale":"en"},"11149":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"**no index**: no index is attached, so **Index strength** has no effect;","locale":"en"},"11150":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"**N speakers**: a voice with several speakers;","locale":"en"},"11151":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"**legacy**: a voice read in place from an original RVC install (see “Original RVC installs” below).","locale":"en"},"11152":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"Tools above the cards:","locale":"en"},"11153":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"**Filter voices**: search by name or tag;","locale":"en"},"11154":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"**Without index**: show only voices without indexes, to help attach missing ones;","locale":"en"},"11155":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"**Show hidden**: show hidden legacy voices.","locale":"en"},"11156":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"Click a card to open the voice's detail page.","locale":"en"},"11157":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"An empty library shows **No voices yet** and a **Get the demo voices** button. Click it to jump to **Assets**, where you can download a few official RVC demo voices to try.","locale":"en"},"11158":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"The top of the detail page has **Back**, **Download** (the voice as a zip: its `.pth`, with the speaker names written in, and its indexes, named so an import pairs them again; also `rvc-next model export`), **Show in folder** (shown only when you open the page on the server machine) and **Delete** buttons. The page has four sections:","locale":"en"},"11159":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**About**","locale":"en"},"11160":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Edit **Name**, **Description** and **Tags** (separated by commas). For voices with several speakers, you can also name each **Speaker N**. Click **Save** when finished.","locale":"en"},"11161":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Below are **Sample rate**, **Version**, **Pitch guidance**, **Speakers**, **File**, **Size** and **Stored info**. Voices with one speaker show **Single speaker · N embedding slots**. Trained voices usually have 109 embedding slots; this does not mean they have several speakers. A voice counts as having several speakers only if speaker information is recorded in the model.","locale":"en"},"11162":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Index**","locale":"en"},"11163":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Lists attached indexes: `default` is the index for the whole voice; `spk<N>` is dedicated to one speaker. Click **Detach** to remove one.","locale":"en"},"11164":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Voices with several speakers show an **Index** dropdown to select whether the next attached index is `default` or a speaker-specific index.","locale":"en"},"11165":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Attach index**: drop an `.index` file here or click to select one.","locale":"en"},"11166":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Server path to an .index**: enter a server path directly, then click **Add** (shown only on the server machine or when an access token is set).","locale":"en"},"11167":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Build from experiment**: select a training experiment and build an index for this voice from its extracted features (the experiment must have completed **Features**).","locale":"en"},"11168":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Every attachment checks that the index fits the voice. Empty indexes with no vectors (the original's `trained_*.index`) and indexes with a mismatched version (256 dimensions for v1, 768 for v2) are rejected.","locale":"en"},"11169":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Default parameters**","locale":"en"},"11170":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Each voice has a default preset, created on import from the default parameters in settings. Selecting the voice on another page automatically loads these parameters. Adjust them here and click **Save**. See Voice parameters for their meanings.","locale":"en"},"11171":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Test**","locale":"en"},"11172":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Convert a short clip with the default parameters.** Select audio and click **Preview 15 s**. Results appear below, ready to play or compare with the source audio.","locale":"en"},"11173":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#delete-and-hide","content":"Library voices: **Delete** asks **Move \\{name} to the trash?** The voice folder is moved to `trash/` in the data folder.","locale":"en"},"11174":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#delete-and-hide","content":"Legacy voices: the button becomes **Hide**, asking **Hide \\{name}? The file in the RVC install is not touched.** Use **Show hidden** to see them again.","locale":"en"},"11175":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#delete-and-hide","content":"Downloaded demo voices: after deletion, you can download them again in **Assets**.","locale":"en"},"11176":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-voice-library-on-disk","content":"By default, the voice library is in `models/` in the data folder (change this in **Settings › Storage › Voices**):","locale":"en"},"11177":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#import-models","content":"The **Voices**, **Base models** and **Separation models** tabs each have a drop zone at the top. All three use the same import workflow, so **any drop zone works**: rvc-next identifies each file by its **contents** (rather than its name or extension), then decides where it belongs.","locale":"en"},"11178":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"File","locale":"en"},"11179":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Identification","locale":"en"},"11180":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"After import","locale":"en"},"11181":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Voice model `.pth` (small model)","locale":"en"},"11182":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Model structure","locale":"en"},"11183":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Added to the voice library","locale":"en"},"11184":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Index `.index`","locale":"en"},"11185":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Vector dimensions: 256 for v1, 768 for v2; no vectors means a `trained_` index","locale":"en"},"11186":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Attached to a paired voice or placed in **Unassigned indexes**","locale":"en"},"11187":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Training generator G (`G_*.pth`)","locale":"en"},"11188":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Version, sample rate and pitch guidance read from weights","locale":"en"},"11189":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Imported as a base model by default; you can also choose **Extract a voice**","locale":"en"},"11190":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Training discriminator D (`D_*.pth`)","locale":"en"},"11191":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Number of sub-discriminators","locale":"en"},"11192":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Paired with G as a base model","locale":"en"},"11193":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Separation model configuration `.yaml` and checkpoint (`.ckpt`, `.pth`, `.bin`, `.safetensors`)","locale":"en"},"11194":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Model type in the configuration","locale":"en"},"11195":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Becomes a separation model and preset","locale":"en"},"11196":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"`.zip`","locale":"en"},"11197":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Extracted files are identified individually","locale":"en"},"11198":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"As above","locale":"en"},"11199":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Unrecognized files are skipped, with **Skipped: …** shown after import.","locale":"en"},"11200":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#import-steps","content":"Drop files into a drop zone (or click to select). You can drop several files at once, such as a `.pth` with its `.index`, or a `.zip` containing both.","locale":"en"},"11201":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#import-steps","content":"A progress bar appears during upload.","locale":"en"},"11202":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#import-steps","content":"If every file's destination is clear, import finishes immediately with a notification such as **Imported \\{names} with 1 index(es)**.","locale":"en"},"11203":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#import-steps","content":"If anything is uncertain, **Review the import** opens for you to confirm before importing.","locale":"en"},"11204":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"Under each drop zone, **Or add from a link** takes one or more links separated by spaces; **Add** has the server download them (a **Download links** job shows the progress), and the import then goes on as for dropped files:","locale":"en"},"11205":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"**Hugging Face**: a file (`…/blob/main/x.pth` or `…/resolve/main/x.pth`), a repository (`huggingface.co/owner/repo`), or a folder in one (`…/tree/main/folder`): every `.pth`, `.index`, `.zip` and separation file in it is downloaded. Hugging Face links go through the Hugging Face endpoint chosen in **Settings › Downloads** (for example hf-mirror); through huggingface.co when the source is ModelScope.","locale":"en"},"11206":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"**Google Drive**: a shared file link (`drive.google.com/file/d/…`). Drive changes how its downloads work from time to time; if a link stops working, download the file in the browser and drop it.","locale":"en"},"11207":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"**Any other link** to a file.","locale":"en"},"11208":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"Links must point at the internet: a link to the server's own machine or its local network (such as `127.0.0.1`, `192.168.…`, `10.…`), including one a site redirects to, is refused, so the web interface cannot be used to reach other services next to the server. The command line (`rvc-next model import <link>`) may download from local addresses. Files over 8 GiB and links that lead to a web page instead of a file are refused. As with any file, a model from the internet is only read as data (see Recognized files); its licence is yours to check.","locale":"en"},"11209":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"Possible notifications after import:","locale":"en"},"11210":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"Message","locale":"en"},"11211":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"11212":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"**Imported \\{names}** / **Imported \\{names} with N index(es)**","locale":"en"},"11213":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"New voices were added to the library","locale":"en"},"11214":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"**Attached \\{names} to voices in your library**","locale":"en"},"11215":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"Indexes were attached to existing library voices","locale":"en"},"11216":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"**Kept \\{names} as unassigned indexes; assign them under Voices.**","locale":"en"},"11217":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"Indexes went to **Unassigned indexes**","locale":"en"},"11218":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"**Imported N base model(s); choose them in an experiment’s settings.**","locale":"en"},"11219":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"Base models were imported","locale":"en"},"11220":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"**Imported N separation model(s); they appear in Separate.**","locale":"en"},"11221":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#links","content":"Separation models were imported","locale":"en"},"11222":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-indexes-are-paired-automatically","content":"Rules for pairing indexes with voices:","locale":"en"},"11223":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-indexes-are-paired-automatically","content":"**Versions must match**: v1 indexes can pair only with v1 voices, v2 only with v2. This is a hard requirement.","locale":"en"},"11224":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-indexes-are-paired-automatically","content":"Compatible voices are scored by name: an exact experiment-name match scores highest, followed by a name containing the voice's name, then similar names. Sharing a folder adds to the score.","locale":"en"},"11225":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-indexes-are-paired-automatically","content":"Automatic pairing happens only when a voice is the index's **only compatible match** in this import, or clearly outscores the other candidates. Otherwise, you choose.","locale":"en"},"11226":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-indexes-are-paired-automatically","content":"Existing library voices are considered only when no suitable voice is in this import.","locale":"en"},"11227":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"The dialog begins with: **Some files could not be paired with certainty. Check the choices below; only compatible voices are offered for each index.** Files are grouped by type:","locale":"en"},"11228":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Voices**: edit each voice's **Name** and use its **Import** switch to decide whether to import it.","locale":"en"},"11229":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Indexes**: each index shows its vector count, pairing state and reasons. Choose a voice in **Voice**—**\\{name} (this import)** or **\\{name} (library)**—or select **Keep unassigned** to put it in unassigned indexes. If the target has several speakers, you can also choose a **Speaker** (default **All speakers**).","locale":"en"},"11230":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Base models and checkpoints**: for each G, select **Use as** **Base model**, **Extract a voice** or **Skip**, and optionally rename it. For a base model, select its paired **Discriminator (D)** (or **None**).","locale":"en"},"11231":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Separation models**: choose a **Checkpoint** for each YAML, enter a name, select **Primary stem** and **Secondary stem** and name them (**Primary name**, **Secondary name**). Use the **Import** switch to decide whether to import it.","locale":"en"},"11232":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Not imported**: unusable files and their reasons, such as **not a model file** or **discriminator without its generator**.","locale":"en"},"11233":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"Index pairing states:","locale":"en"},"11234":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"State","locale":"en"},"11235":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"11236":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Only match**","locale":"en"},"11237":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"Only one compatible voice","locale":"en"},"11238":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Matched**","locale":"en"},"11239":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"A match was found by name or folder","locale":"en"},"11240":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Choose**","locale":"en"},"11241":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"Several candidates; you must choose","locale":"en"},"11242":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**No fit**","locale":"en"},"11243":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"No voice with a matching version","locale":"en"},"11244":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Empty**","locale":"en"},"11245":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"No vectors (a `trained_` index); cannot be used","locale":"en"},"11246":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Duplicate**","locale":"en"},"11247":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"Another index fits the same voice better","locale":"en"},"11248":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"**Chosen**","locale":"en"},"11249":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"You selected a match manually","locale":"en"},"11250":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#review-the-import-dialog","content":"Click **Import** to confirm. **Cancel** abandons this import and discards the uploaded files.","locale":"en"},"11251":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#unassigned-indexes","content":"Indexes without a paired voice appear in **Unassigned indexes** at the top of **Voices**: **Indexes imported without a voice. Only voices of the matching version are offered.**","locale":"en"},"11252":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#unassigned-indexes","content":"Select a voice in **Voice** (only matching versions are listed). For voices with several speakers, you can also select a **Speaker**.","locale":"en"},"11253":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#unassigned-indexes","content":"Click **Assign**.","locale":"en"},"11254":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#unassigned-indexes","content":"Click Delete for indexes you do not need.","locale":"en"},"11255":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#unassigned-indexes","content":"If the library has no voice of the same version, a message such as **No v1 voice in the library yet** appears.","locale":"en"},"11256":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#applio","content":"Applio, another RVC application, writes a few extra details into its voices; rvc-next reads them:","locale":"en"},"11257":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#applio","content":"Voices with Applio's default vocoder (HiFi-GAN) are RVC voices and work as they are. Their author, epoch, step and training length appear in **About**; a multi-speaker voice gets numbered speakers you can rename.","locale":"en"},"11258":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#applio","content":"A voice trained on another **content-feature model** (Applio's \"embedder\": SPIN, SPIN v2, or the Chinese, Japanese or Korean HuBERT) converts with that model, as it was trained. **About** shows **Content features**; the first conversion asks to download the model (about 380 MB, from Applio's repository; also under **Assets › Content-feature models**).","locale":"en"},"11259":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#applio","content":"Voices with Applio's **RefineGAN** or **MRF HiFi-GAN** vocoders, and voices trained on a custom content-feature model, cannot be used: importing one says why, and it is skipped.","locale":"en"},"11260":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#original-rvc-installs","content":"If you still have the original RVC, you can use its voices directly without copying models. The **Original RVC installs** section at the bottom of **Voices** says: **Voices in an RVC install are used in place; Import all copies them into the library.**","locale":"en"},"11261":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#original-rvc-installs","content":"Click **Add an RVC install**.","locale":"en"},"11262":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#original-rvc-installs","content":"Enter the original's root directory in **RVC folder** (it should contain an `assets` folder), or click **Browse…** to select it.","locale":"en"},"11263":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#original-rvc-installs","content":"Click **Add**.","locale":"en"},"11264":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#original-rvc-installs","content":"rvc-next reads voices in `assets/weights` and recommends an index for each from `assets/indices` and `logs`, following the original's rules. These voices are marked **legacy**. Files stay in place; rvc-next never writes to the original's folders (indexes attached to legacy voices are copied to `models/attached-indexes/`).","locale":"en"},"11265":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#original-rvc-installs","content":"Each added install has two buttons:","locale":"en"},"11266":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#original-rvc-installs","content":"**Scan**: rereads models after additions or deletions in the original and recommends indexes for new voices (voices whose indexes you selected manually are unaffected);","locale":"en"},"11267":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#original-rvc-installs","content":"**Import all**: copies all voices and their indexes from this install into the library, where they can be edited like ordinary voices.","locale":"en"},"11268":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#original-rvc-installs","content":"See Migrate from the original RVC for more details.","locale":"en"},"11269":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#base-models","content":"The **Base models** tab says: **Training starts from a base model. Download the official ones below, or import your own G (and D); their rate, version and pitch guidance are read from the weights.**","locale":"en"},"11270":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#base-models","content":"**Import base models**: drop G and D `.pth` files, or a `.zip`. G and D are paired automatically by name; G alone can also be imported (shown as **no D**).","locale":"en"},"11271":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#base-models","content":"**Your base models**: imported models show version · sample rate · pitch guidance · **G + D** or **no D** · size. You can **Rename** or Delete them (moving them to the trash).","locale":"en"},"11272":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#base-models","content":"**Community base models**: 21 base models trained by RVC users (KLM, Snowie, Titan, Ov2Super, Rigel and others; the list Applio keeps), all v2 with pitch guidance. Each row shows its licence as its repository states it (many state none: check before you share what you train) and the repository it comes from; **Download** fetches it from there (about 1.3 GB, G and D). Once downloaded, it can be chosen as an experiment's base model.","locale":"en"},"11273":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#base-models","content":"**Official**: official base models for v1/v2 × 32k/40k/48k × with/without pitch guidance. **Download** fetches the full set for that version and sample rate (4 files: G and D with and without pitch guidance). Deleting removes only that entry's own G and D; you can download them again later.","locale":"en"},"11274":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#base-models","content":"A training experiment's **Settings › Base model** lists only models matching its sample rate, version and pitch guidance. See Train.","locale":"en"},"11275":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#separation-models","content":"The **Separation models** tab says: **The built-in models are downloaded here or in Assets; import your own as a checkpoint with its YAML config. Each becomes a preset in Separate.**","locale":"en"},"11276":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#separation-models","content":"**Import separation models**: drop a checkpoint (`.ckpt`, `.pth`, `.safetensors`) with its `.yaml`, or a `.zip`. Before importing, rvc-next actually loads the model once to check it works (this may take a few seconds).","locale":"en"},"11277":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#separation-models","content":"**Your separation models**: shows model type, primary/secondary stem names and size; models can be deleted. Each imported model becomes a preset marked **imported** on **Separate**.","locale":"en"},"11278":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#separation-models","content":"**Built-in**: built-in separation models, each marked **presets: …** to show which separation presets use it. You can download or delete them.","locale":"en"},"11279":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#separation-models","content":"With no imported models, the page shows **No separation models imported**. Built-in presets are always available on **Separate**.","locale":"en"},"11280":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"**Assets** lists every file rvc-next can download, grouped by purpose:","locale":"en"},"11281":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"Group","locale":"en"},"11282":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"Files","locale":"en"},"11283":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"Approximate size","locale":"en"},"11284":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"**Conversion**","locale":"en"},"11285":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"HuBERT (required for all conversion, Live and training), RMVPE, RMVPE (ONNX, for DirectML devices), FCPE, CREPE, CREPE tiny","locale":"en"},"11286":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"180 MB, 173 MB, 345 MB, 41 MB, 85 MB, 2 MB","locale":"en"},"11287":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"**Training**","locale":"en"},"11288":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"Official base models v1/v2 × 32k/40k/48k","locale":"en"},"11289":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"About 350–420 MB per group","locale":"en"},"11290":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"**Separation**","locale":"en"},"11291":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"Vocals, Vocals (aggressive), Dereverb, Dereverb (aggressive), Lead vocals","locale":"en"},"11292":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"About 305–436 MB each","locale":"en"},"11293":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"File names and descriptions come from the server in English, for example `HuBERT`, `Base models v2 40k`, `Separation: Vocals`.","locale":"en"},"11294":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"Each row shows name, description, size (checked files are marked **verified**) and state: **Installed**, **Not installed**, **Partly downloaded**, **Checksum mismatch**, **Downloading**. Available actions:","locale":"en"},"11295":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"**Download**: starts a download. While downloading, a progress bar and “downloaded / total size · speed · time remaining” appear.","locale":"en"},"11296":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"**Download everything for Conversion** (also **Download everything for Training**, **Download everything for Separation**): buttons beside group headings download all missing files in that group at once.","locale":"en"},"11297":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"**Verify**: recalculates SHA-256 checksums for installed files.","locale":"en"},"11298":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"Delete: removes files; you can download them again later. Files cannot be deleted during a download.","locale":"en"},"11299":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"Downloads resume after interruption (unfinished files end in `.part`), retry automatically on failure and verify checksums on completion. You do not need to download everything in advance: whenever a page needs a file, the relevant button is replaced by **Needs …** and **Download (size)**.","locale":"en"},"11300":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#assets","content":"Configure downloads in **Settings › Downloads**: switch **Model repository** between rvc-model and the official RVC repository, or change **Download source** to ModelScope, hf-mirror.com or a custom mirror. See “Downloads” in Settings.","locale":"en"},"11301":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#demo-voices","content":"At the bottom of **Assets** is **Demo voices**: **The official RVC example voices, downloaded from the model repository with their indexes.** Each row shows sample rate · version · **with index** · size.","locale":"en"},"11302":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#demo-voices","content":"Click **Download** for one voice, or **Download all**. It then says **Download started; the voice appears in the library when it is ready.**","locale":"en"},"11303":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#demo-voices","content":"Downloaded voices show an **In library** button; click it to open their detail page.","locale":"en"},"11304":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#demo-voices","content":"Demo voices are stored only in rvc-model, so they always download from rvc-model regardless of the selected **Model repository**.","locale":"en"},"11305":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#merge-two-voices","content":"Combine two voices into a new one using weights:","locale":"en"},"11306":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#merge-two-voices","content":"Select **First voice** and **Second voice**. Their sample rate, version and pitch guidance must match.","locale":"en"},"11307":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#merge-two-voices","content":"Adjust **Weight of the first voice** (0–1, default 0.5): result = weight × first + (1 − weight) × second.","locale":"en"},"11308":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-195","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#merge-two-voices","content":"Enter a **New voice name** and click **Merge**.","locale":"en"},"11309":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-196","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#merge-two-voices","content":"Merging runs as a background job. The new voice appears in the library when finished.","locale":"en"},"11310":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-197","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#extract-a-voice-from-a-checkpoint","content":"Training checkpoints (`G_*.pth`) cannot be used directly for conversion; extract a small model first:","locale":"en"},"11311":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-198","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#extract-a-voice-from-a-checkpoint","content":"In **Checkpoint (G\\_\\*.pth path or \\<experiment>/\\<file>)**, enter the checkpoint's full server path, or use `experiment-name/G_xxx.pth` to refer to a checkpoint in an experiment.","locale":"en"},"11312":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-199","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#extract-a-voice-from-a-checkpoint","content":"Enter a **New voice name**.","locale":"en"},"11313":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-200","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#extract-a-voice-from-a-checkpoint","content":"**Sample rate** and **Model version** default to **From the experiment**. If the checkpoint is outside an experiment and these cannot be read, select them manually.","locale":"en"},"11314":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-201","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#extract-a-voice-from-a-checkpoint","content":"Click **Extract**. The new voice appears in the library when finished.","locale":"en"},"11315":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-202","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#extract-a-voice-from-a-checkpoint","content":"For trained voices, **Export as voice** in **Train › Results** is usually easier: it extracts the voice automatically and includes the index.","locale":"en"},"11316":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-203","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#command-line","content":"When a command-line import encounters uncertain pairings, it prints the plan and exits with code 3. Use `--pair`, `--keep-unassigned` and `--extract` to decide. See Command reference for full details.","locale":"en"},"11317":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"page","content":"Voice parameters","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","locale":"en"},"11318":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","content":"Voice parameters determine the converted sound: pitch, formant, pitch method, index strength, consonant protection and loudness match, plus the speaker for multi-speaker voices. RVC Next uses the same parameter panel in Convert, Live and Default parameters in voice details, with identical names, ranges, defaults, help and order. The command line and API use the same parameters and ranges.","locale":"en"},"11319":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#parameter-panel","content":"Parameter panel","locale":"en"},"11320":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#parameters-at-a-glance","content":"Parameters at a glance","locale":"en"},"11321":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#f0","content":"Pitch method","locale":"en"},"11322":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#pitch","content":"Pitch","locale":"en"},"11323":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#formant","content":"Formant","locale":"en"},"11324":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#index-rate","content":"Index strength","locale":"en"},"11325":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#protect","content":"Consonant protection","locale":"en"},"11326":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#unvoiced","content":"Frames without pitch","locale":"en"},"11327":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#high-register","content":"Very high notes","locale":"en"},"11328":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#auto-pitch","content":"Automatic key","locale":"en"},"11329":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#autotune","content":"Autotune","locale":"en"},"11330":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#rms-mix","content":"Loudness match","locale":"en"},"11331":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#speaker","content":"Speaker","locale":"en"},"11332":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#presets","content":"Presets","locale":"en"},"11333":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#each-voices-default-preset","content":"Each voice's default preset","locale":"en"},"11334":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#apply-a-preset","content":"Apply a preset","locale":"en"},"11335":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#save-a-preset","content":"Save a preset","locale":"en"},"11336":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#live","content":"Parameters in live voice conversion","locale":"en"},"11337":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","content":"This page explains each parameter and how to use presets.","locale":"en"},"11338":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#parameter-panel","content":"The panel is titled **Voice parameters** and contains:","locale":"en"},"11339":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#parameter-panel","content":"**Pitch method**: a menu of the pitch methods;","locale":"en"},"11340":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#parameter-panel","content":"Five sliders: **Pitch**, **Formant**, **Index strength**, **Consonant protection** and **Loudness match**;","locale":"en"},"11341":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#parameter-panel","content":"**Pitch details**, a section that opens on click, with **Frames without pitch**, **Very high notes**, **Automatic key** and **Autotune**;","locale":"en"},"11342":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-parameters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-parameters#parameter-panel","content":"The **Presets** menu at the to