ph`, `enable_asio`, backend)"],[3384,"`WorkerRequest`（地址、authkey、资源目录、设备、精度、`cuda_graph`、`enable_asio`、后端）"],[8237,"`workers.live` is the exception: it persists and needs two-way communication, so it uses `multiprocessing.connection`. Core's `LiveSupervisor` opens a `Listener` with a random authkey and writes its address into the request file; the two sides then exchange JSON messages defined in `protocol/live.py` (`Start`, `UpdateVoice`, `SetDevices`… and `State`, `Stats`, `DeviceLost`, `Log`). See Core services and Engine."],[2102,"`workers.live` 例外：它长驻，需要双向通信，所以走 `multiprocessing.connection`。核心层的 `LiveSupervisor` 开一个带随机 authkey 的 `Listener`，把地址写进请求文件；之后双方交换 `protocol/live.py` 中定义的 JSON 消息（`Start`、`UpdateVoice`、`SetDevices`……以及 `State`、`Stats`、`DeviceLost`、`Log`）。详见核心服务与引擎。"],[8731,"`workers.separate` subprocess"],[2596,"`workers.separate` 子进程"],[9663,"`workers.train` and training service"],[3528,"`workers.train` 与训练服务"],[2604,"`workers.train` 的 `index` 阶段"],[8230,"`workers.train`, `workers.separate` and `workers.devices` follow the same conventions, derived from the event protocol in the original's `tools/pymss_webui.py`:"],[2095,"`workers.train`、`workers.separate` 和 `workers.devices` 遵循同一套约定，源自原版 `tools/pymss_webui.py` 的事件协议："],[3863,"`workers/`"],[9998,"`workers/`"],[9428,"`workers/live.py` is a persistent process owning audio devices and real-time threads, isolated from the server's event loop, GIL contention and crashes. It connects back to core with `multiprocessing.connection.Client` (address and random authkey in the request file, `protocol/live.py:WorkerRequest`), exchanging JSON messages defined in `protocol/live.py`."],[3293,"`workers/live.py` 是一个长期运行的进程，拥有音频设备和实时线程，与服务器的事件循环、GIL 竞争和崩溃隔离。它用 `multiprocessing.connection.Client` 连回核心层（地址和随机 authkey 在请求文件里，`protocol/live.py:WorkerRequest`），收发 `protocol/live.py` 定义的 JSON 消息。"],[1990,"`workers`"],[8125,"`workers`"],[3061,"`x_center`"],[9196,"`x_center`"],[3062,"`x_max`"],[9197,"`x_max`"],[3059,"`x_pad`"],[919