13"],[3075,"6"],[9210,"6"],[3071,"60"],[9206,"60"],[3072,"65"],[9207,"65"],[1703,"7"],[2147,"7"],[7838,"7"],[8282,"7"],[1706,"8"],[2152,"8"],[7841,"8"],[8287,"8"],[1709,"9"],[2157,"9"],[7844,"9"],[8292,"9"],[6619,"A \"—\" in the \"Default\" column means the option has no effect unless supplied, or inherits a value from a preset or settings (as explained in the description). Ranges are written as `[a, b]`."],[7762,"A \"device selection\" is an object: `device_id` (empty follows the system default), `physical_key`, `name`, `host_api`, `channels` (input channels to mix down to mono, numbered from 1; output channels to write to; empty uses the first input channel and first two output channels), `sample_rate`, and `exclusive` (WASAPI exclusive mode). These are usually selected in the Web UI's device panel or written by `rvc-next live run --input/--output`; manual editing is unnecessary."],[10568,"A **Play** button: all results share one player, so playing one stops the other;"],[11955,"A **Problems** list (**No problems found** when there are none):"],[7000,"A `G_*.pth` checkpoint, or `<experiment>/<file>` (required)"],[9021,"A `SetDevices` that changes only gains or the monitor's source updates the running `AudioSession.config` in place (`SessionConfig.same_endpoints`); other changes reopen the devices."],[9986,"A 1.5-second, 22050 Hz `tone()`, written to `tmp_path/src/speech.wav`"],[11056,"A bar stays fixed at the bottom of the page:"],[10132,"A card grows into a dialog"],[11858,"A color picker, any color"],[11913,"A dataset with several speakers is described by a **Speakers** table, with one speaker per row:"],[8352,"A demo voice; `size`, `has_index`, and `repositories` (repositories hosting all its files) are computed at load time"],[8451,"A download job is processing it"],[10995,"A driver that starts the stream and then ends it by itself within its first moments (about 0.4 s, or two blocks when they are longer) counts as a refusal too: the next driver is tried, rather than Live waiting for the device to come back. Starting, the meter and **Hear yourself** take that much longer on a device with several drivers."],[8565,"A few commands choose exit codes themselves, consistently with domain errors: `webui` exits 4 when a certificate file is missing and 3 when no port is available; `model import` prints an ambiguous import plan and exits 3; `live check` / `live run` exit 8 for device problems. CLI-only argument validation uses `typer.BadParameter` (exit code 2)."],[12246,"A few designs shared throughout the application:"],[10190,"A few more conventions:"],[10559,"A few special cases:"],[6162,"A host program usually has its own configuration folder; RVC Next's settings can go there while the data stays in the data folder:"],[8343,"A Hugging Face repository. `selected` is computed from settings, not stored in the catalog"],[10400,"A job card appears in the action bar, showing status and progress. Once complete, the output appears in **Results**:"],[8719,"A job kind registers a factory with `JobService.register(kind, factory)`: `request dict → JobSpec(title, run, resources, steps, priority)`. The request itself (plain JSON) is stored in the `jobs.request` column, so **Retry** can resubmit the same request after a server restart (`retry()` is `submit(job.kind, job.request)`). Factories should revalidate requests because a voice or file may have changed by retry time."],[10912,"A long list (nine items or more, usual on Windows) has a search field at the top."],[9648,"A map for diagnosing issues against the original."],[11239,"A match was found by name or folder"],[6138,"A minimal example"],[11947,"A noise gate over each recording before it is cut, for noisy recordings; separating with **Clean the dataset first** removes more (music, reverb)"],[10990,"A note may also appear below a device explaining how the saved device was found again, such as **\\{name} was found under another driver.** (a different driver, but the same device), or **\\{name} was not found: using the system default.**"],[10669,"A PipeWire / PulseAudio virtual microphone"],[11534,"A preset is a saved set of voice parameters (excluding speaker). Each preset either **belongs to one voice** or is shared by **all voices**."],[8910,"A previous output itself, or the input used to produce it"],[11201,"A progress bar appears during upload."],[10549,"A progress bar while running; download jobs also show downloaded/total size, speed and time remaining."],[10996,"A refused permission (the microphone blocked in the system's privacy settings) is not retried: it blocks every driver alike."],[8108,"A request's path"],[10476,"A reverb or delay rings out past the end of the voice: the result is longer by its audible tail."],[12087,"A selected G checkpoint is first extracted into a small model;"],[6528,"A self-signed certificate works after the browser's warning is accepted (`openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -keyout key.pem -out cert.pem -days 365 -subj /CN=my-pc`). A reverse proxy that terminates HTTPS works too; it must forward the WebSocket at `/api/v1/live/browser-audio` as well as those under `/ws/`."],[9243,"A separate CUDA Graph namespace for each of the four combinations (version × mask present/absent)."],[8849,"A session is `uploads/imports/<sid>/`, containing `session.json` and `files/<file id>/<original filename>`; creating a session also removes old sessions idle for 24 hours (`SESSION_TTL`)."],[10135,"A side sheet slides in from an edge"],[12073,"A single stage: click **Run this stage** on its card. Completed stages show **Run again**, which forces another run."],[9938,"A small-model `.pth` (fp16 weights, `enc_q` removed), written with `write_small_model`"],[7391,"A state (`queued`, `waiting`, `running`, `cancelling`, `cancelled`, `failed`, `completed`, `interrupted`), or `active`, `finished`"],[9947,"A torchfcpe-format FCPE checkpoint (`config_dict`, `model`, output weights using old `weight_g` / `weight_v` keys)"],[11274,"A training experiment's **Settings › Base model** lists only models matching its sample rate, version and pitch guidance. See Train."],[9941,"A training G checkpoint (`model`, `iteration`, `optimizer`, `learning_rate`)"],[10179,"A translated title by error code, the original server message, and expandable “Details” (`errorView` in `errors.ts`); tracebacks only appear in job logs"],[8346,"A unit that can be downloaded and have its status determined independently"],[12178,"A venv or standalone Python dedicated to RVC Next; **do not** share it with other applications"],[11439,"A very small, very fast neural pitch model (about 100× real time on one CPU core) that its benchmark puts level with RMVPE, up to 2093 Hz; a repair step from Applio lifts notes it briefly reads an octave low"],[8575,"A voice can be specified by ID, name, or `.pth` path. With a path, `convert` uses `services.models.temporary()` to register a **temporary voice** (`tmp-…`, hidden from lists), with an optional index supplied by `--index`; parameters start from `convert.default_params` rather than the voice's default preset. `live run` only accepts library voices (`resolve(..., allow_path=False)`): `LiveConfig` identifies the voice by ID, saved as `live.last_voice` after startup so the next `live run` without `--voice` and the Web UI can restore the session."],[6820,"A voice id from `tts voices` (required)"],[8839,"A voice is multi-speaker only when its `.pth` has `speaker_info` (or the user has named speakers). Every trained voice has 109 speaker embedding rows; using row count would make every voice multi-speaker (AGENTS.md §8). `speaker_slots` still reports embedding row count to validate `speaker_id` ranges. Speaker names live in `voice.json` (`legacy-voices.json` for legacy voices), without modifying `.pth`."],[8796,"A voice is the unit users choose throughout the app: a small model, its indexes, speakers and default parameters. `VoiceModelService` (`core/models/service.py`) manages them."],[12245,"A voice library, indexes, base models, separation models, required asset downloads and tools for merging voices and extracting voices from checkpoints"],[11258,"A voice trained on another **content-feature model** (Applio's \"embedder\": SPIN, SPIN v2, or the Chinese, Japanese or Korean HuBERT) converts with that model, as it was trained. **About** shows **Content features**; the first conversion asks to download the model (about 380 MB, from Applio's repository; also under **Assets › Content-feature models**)."],[6226,"A voice with speaker information in its `.pth` is multi-speaker. Its card shows **N speakers**, and the parameter panel includes a **Speaker** option. On the command line, use `--speaker <id>`; `rvc-next model info <voice> --speakers` lists speakers. You can name them with `rvc-next model edit <voice> --speaker-name 0=Alice`. Multi-speaker voices can also have a separate index for each speaker (`--speaker`). Live voice conversion uses the selected speaker too."],[11469,"A voice's index (`.index` file) stores features from its training data. During conversion, RVC finds the features closest to the input and mixes them in at this ratio, making the result closer to the training voice."],[11688,"About"],[11292,"About 305–436 MB each"],[11289,"About 350–420 MB per group"],[6363,"Above 80% load, the bar turns red and shows **Increase block to \\{ms} ms** (the suggested value targets about 70% load, capped at 1500 milliseconds). Click to apply;"],[7874,"Access control"],[7978,"Access control has two layers: `SecurityMiddleware` handles who can connect, while `require_local` in routes guards operations that only make sense for a browser on the server machine."],[7989,"Access token"],[10527,"Access token"],[11678,"Access token"],[6452,"Access token (optional)"],[7486,"Access token; once set, all API and WebSocket requests must carry it"],[11647,"Accompaniment"],[6740,"Accompaniment gain in dB"],[10965,"Action"],[10124,"Actual use"],[7812,"Add `--help` at any level to see help. Entering just a group name (such as `rvc-next model`) also shows that group's help."],[8096,"Add a route in the appropriate `api/routers/<resource>.py`: set `operation_id`, use `ServicesDep` in the signature, and add `dependencies=[LocalDep]` for revealing files; use `spool` + `read_chunks` for uploads and declare `openapi_extra=RAW_BODY`. Put fixed paths before wildcard routes."],[11594,"Add audio in **Inputs**: drop files, click **Server files** to choose server files or an entire folder (processing audio files at its top level), or click **Earlier results**. This works exactly as on Convert's input section."],[8511,"Add demo voices to `voices`; never change an `id` once published, since downloaded voices use it to match catalog entries."],[11122,"Add from a link"],[10413,"Add inputs"],[10489,"Add inputs, choose a voice and set **Pitch**;"],[10786,"Add one of these blocks to `~/.asoundrc` (create the file if it doesn't exist; keep anything already in it). Choose by what rvc-next's **Output** menu already lists: **pipewire** means the PipeWire ALSA plugin is installed (package `pipewire-alsa`), **pulse** means the PulseAudio one (`libasound2-plugins` on Debian and Ubuntu, `alsa-plugins-pulseaudio` on Fedora, `alsa-plugins` on Arch)."],[8508,"Add or update an entry in `assets` in `catalog.json`: `path` uses a relative path in the original `assets/` layout; `sources` lists at least one repository; `size` and `sha256` must match the manifest—downloads use size to determine completion and hashes to detect corruption."],[6737,"Add the accompaniment back (needs `--separate`)"],[8593,"Add the command to the user documentation's Command reference."],[10584,"Add this result to the current page's inputs for another pass"],[6516,"Added original RVC installations;"],[11183,"Added to the voice library"],[8522,"Adding a command"],[10038,"Adding a screen"],[10469,"Adding accompaniment back produces stereo output; if mixing would clip, the overall level is aut