ation\" (`paths.legacy_roots` in settings), its voices are **read directly without copying**:"],[11543,"After adjusting parameters, click **Presets** › **Save as preset**."],[10739,"After changing devices in Windows, or if a strip stays silent, use **Menu › Restart Audio Engine**."],[11780,"After changing folders or browsable locations, click **Save** at the bottom right."],[11660,"After choosing a preset, if its models are not downloaded, the **Separate** button in the action bar is replaced by a notice such as “**Needs Separation: Vocals**” and a **Download** button. Click to download."],[10497,"After clicking, you can continue changing parameters or inputs and submit again; the new job is queued afterward. See Interface overview › Jobs for general information about jobs."],[9461,"After device loss, the worker reports `DeviceLost`, stops the session and enters `reconnecting`, then waits for `SetDevices`; core handles re-enumeration and reopening on `exact`/`matched` (see Core services). On a processing-thread error or OOM during loading/prewarming, the worker unloads all its models first, then reports `compute_unavailable` (`detail.reason = \"out_of_memory\"`)."],[9027,"After every actual change, `SettingsService` calculates changed dotted keys with `changed_keys()`, notifying `on_change` (new settings) and `on_keys_change` (key names). Changes can come from `update()` or another process writing `settings.toml`: reading `settings` compares mtime and size at most once per `FILE_CHECK_INTERVAL` (1 second), rereading on change (parse or validation failures log a warning and retain previous settings); `update()` forces a check before writing, merging onto current file contents. The key listener registered in `core/context.py` publishes `settings_changed` and calls `models.rescan()` when `paths.*` changes."],[8072,"After FastAPI generates its schema, `RvcNextAPI.openapi()` in `api/openapi.py` adds each event class's JSON Schema (`mode=\"serialization\"`) to `components.schemas`, promotes nested `$defs` to peer components, and adds a `ServerEvents` object: property names are event names, and values reference event schemas. Components are sorted by name for stable output."],[11180,"After import"],[10317,"After installing RVC Next, follow the entire first-run process: start the web interface, learn where data is stored, download HuBERT and RMVPE for conversion, get a demo voice and complete a conversion. Each step includes both web interface and command-line instructions."],[7778,"After its first start, the live worker stays running until the server exits. These settings are read when it starts, so changes require a server restart"],[9412,"Aliases following system defaults, such as `Microsoft Sound Mapper` and `Primary Sound Driver`, are omitted; virtual devices (VB-Audio, VoiceMeeter, BlackHole, Loopback, Soundflower, null sink…) get `is_virtual`."],[7392,"All"],[9051,"All `AssetStatus`"],[12263,"All `rvc-next` commands, configuration files and environment variables"],[6610,"All commands accept these options, which are omitted from the tables below:"],[8363,"All conversion and feature extraction (transformers format)"],[9682,"All conversion in the callback; `skip_head`/`return_length`; 1024-frame pitch cache"],[11145,"All downloadable files: HuBERT, the pitch models (RMVPE, FCPE, CREPE), base models, separation models and demo voices"],[6518,"All drives (`C:\\`, `D:\\`, etc. on Windows), or mounted volumes (`/Volumes/*` on macOS; `/media/<user>/*`, `/run/media/<user>/*`, `/mnt/*` on Linux). The system root `/` is excluded by default."],[9383,"All entry points share an `RLock`, so control-thread updates cannot interleave with the processing thread's `process()`."],[9703,"All existing user models; models written by rvc-next also work in the original"],[8438,"All files copied from the official repository are unchanged; catalog hashes were recalculated against a full download of the official repository (revision `e6d0c1a`) and all matched."],[8455,"All files exist, but one failed verification"],[7968,"All fixed paths in `routers/models.py` (`/catalog`, `/imports`, `/indexes`, `/base`, `/separation`, `/legacy-roots`…) precede `/{voice_id}`. FastAPI matches in registration order: new fixed paths must go above wildcard routes, or they will be treated as voice IDs. The same applies to `POST /zip` in `outputs`."],[9501,"All four workers use `python -m rvc_next.workers.<name> <request.json>` and share `workers/base.py:run_worker()`:"],[8848,"All import entry points—the Web UI drop zones, `PUT /models/imports/{sid}/files`, `POST /models/imports/{sid}/paths`, `rvc-next model import`, old one-step `PUT /models/import` and `POST /models/import-path`—use the same import session (`core/models/imports.py`). The goal: correctly pair `.pth` and `.index` files even when their names are unrelated, and independently import four model types (voices, indexes, base models, separation models)."],[9343,"All lengths use the device sample rate `sample_rate`, with `zc = sample_rate // 100` (10 ms); millisecond parameters are rounded to whole 10 ms units (`_frames`, the original's rounding):"],[8504,"All remaining model files in the archives are byte-identical to a file in the repository."],[10171,"All screens"],[10180,"All screens"],[7426,"All settings"],[11873,"All settings can also be viewed and changed from the command line. Changes are written to the same `settings.toml`:"],[7175,"All stages that need to run"],[10740,"All Voicemeeter devices run at A1's sample rate. Set Voicemeeter's playback and recording devices to the same format (48000 Hz) in the Sound Control Panel; then rvc-next shows **one duplex stream** when your microphone uses 48 kHz too."],[9295,"All writes use `torch_save()`, writing `.tmp` then `os.replace`, so a crash cannot leave a partial model."],[9269,"All; CPU on DirectML"],[9273,"All; CPU on DirectML"],[9265,"All; mel and decoding on CPU for DirectML"],[6451,"Allow other computers to connect"],[10