n GPU memory. It is available whenever no jobs or live voice conversion are running; otherwise, it is disabled and shows the reason, such as “Free GPU memory (wait: a job is running)”. Success is reported as “GPU memory freed”."],[10894,"Closing the tab, or losing the connection for 3 seconds, stops the session. Only one browser can be connected at a time: a newer one takes over."],[9751,"Code conventions at a glance"],[9759,"Code on **the original's side** of the golden tests (the original's live code imports torchaudio, and its FCPE imports torchfcpe)."],[10065,"Color"],[11914,"Column"],[11305,"Combine two voices into a new one using weights:"],[8531,"Command functions: plain functions without decorators"],[8198,"Command line"],[11135,"Command line"],[11591,"Command line"],[11888,"Command line"],[12262,"Command line"],[6224,"Command line: `rvc-next model index attach <voice> <file>`, or `rvc-next model index build <voice> --experiment <experiment>`."],[6545,"Command reference"],[7866,"Command reference: parameters and options for all commands."],[9997,"Command tree snapshot, `--debug` at each level, `config`, `--json` parity with the API, conversion by `.pth` path, missing-asset exit codes"],[6358,"Command-line jobs (`rvc-next convert`, etc.) run in their own processes and do not participate in a running server's GPU queue. Running a GPU job from the command line on the same computer while the server is doing live voice conversion can also cause audio glitches."],[6462,"Command-line option"],[11351,"Command-line option"],[7796,"Commands at a glance"],[8587,"Commands listing or displaying data provide `--json` and print the core method's `Record` directly."],[8568,"Commands obtain services with `with open_services() as services:`. Its call to `build_services()` **starts no background threads**: no scheduler, idle unloading, or Live worker supervision. Services close when the command finishes."],[8617,"Commit"],[10327,"Common options for `rvc-next webui`:"],[6192,"C