"Device latency here is what PortAudio reports, which is often optimistic (MME, DirectSound and Bluetooth devices especially). For the real figure, connect the output to the input and use **Measure latency** on the Live page or `rvc-next live latency`: it plays noise bursts through the same buffers a session uses, finds them in the input by cross-correlation, and adds the converter's own delay. See Measure the real latency."],[9517,"Device list, or `{ok, reason, message, role, …}`"],[10909,"Device menus are arranged as follows:"],[10624,"Device names"],[7384,"Device names can be full names or substrings, as long as they match exactly one device. If multiple devices match, use an ID from `live devices`. A device given by name (or `default`) uses the automatic driver (Automatic driver); an ID names one driver's variant and uses that driver alone. After starting, the devices, buffering parameters, voice, and voice parameters are saved as defaults for next time."],[10866,"Device problems and repair buttons"],[7691,"Device selection"],[7695,"Device selection"],[10182,"Device selection: full physical device names, server hostname in the title, input meter, test tone, optional monitor output, drivers under “Advanced”, problems beside the affected device; options are built in unit-testable `devices.ts`"],[7699,"Device selection?"],[11724,"Device used to run models. The dropdown lists detected devices and their GPU memory; unsupported devices are marked ✕. Automatic selects the most suitable NVIDIA GPU (highest compute capability, most GPU memory), then tries DirectML, then CPU. You can also choose a specific GPU (`cuda:N`), DirectML, CPU or experimental Apple MPS (`mps`)"],[9999,"Device worker (enumeration, format checks, test tones, and real local PortAudio enumeration); Live worker (start, hot updates, voice switches, reconnect after device loss, nonfatal errors, meters / passthrough / test tones, end-to-end process, idle release and OOM unloading); separation worker (chain events with a fake separator, no overwriting existing files, individual input failure, missing weights, fp32 retry requested after DirectML fp16 failure, cancellation by process kill); training worker (slice → F0 → features → index)"],[8164,"Device, GPU memory usage, GPU lease, idle unloading"],[8633,"Devices"],[10998,"Devices chosen before this option existed keep working: one saved on the recommended driver is treated as **Auto**, one saved on another driver keeps that driver."],[7797,"Differences from the Web UI"],[135,"DirectML"],[6270,"DirectML"],[6293,"DirectML (AMD, Intel, and other GPUs on Windows). Falls back to CPU if unavailable"],[12197,"DirectML is a fallback for AMD and Intel GPUs on Windows that the ROCm and XPU builds above do not support. Install PyTorch as shown under “CPU only”, then install RVC Next with the `directml` extra in step 3:"],[2236,"DirectML 上的 RMVPE"],[6062,"DirectML 是备用方案，用于上面的 ROCm 和 XPU 构建不支持的 Windows AMD 和 Intel 显卡。先按“仅 CPU”安装 PyTorch，再在第三步安装带 `directml` 附加项的 RVC Next："],[6313,"DirectML, MPS, and CPU always use fp32 (except vocal separation on DirectML; see below). fp16 is faster and uses less GPU memory; if a card produces abnormal output in fp16, switch to `fp32`."],[178,"DirectML、MPS 和 CPU 上始终是 fp32（DirectML 上的人声分离例外，见下）。fp16 更快、显存占用更少；如果某块卡在 fp16 下输出异常，改为 `fp32`。"],[158,"DirectML（Windows 上的 AMD、Intel 等显卡）。不可用时退回 CPU"],[8413,"Directory"],[9988,"Directory"],[10029,"Directory structure"],[9291,"Discriminators are `MultiPeriodDiscriminator` (v1) and `MultiPeriodDiscriminatorV2` (v2)."],[8607,"Disk layout and database cache"],[12181,"Disk space"],[7985,"DNS rebinding: a malicious page resolves its own domain to 127.0.0.1 and calls the local API"],[1850,"DNS 重绑定：恶意网页把自己的域名解析到 127.0.0.1 后调用本机 API"],[6976,"Do not ask for confirmation"],[9873,"Do not name a method `list` on a class with `list[...]` annotations (ty resolves `list` to that method): use names such as `list_assets`, `list_jobs`, `list_voices`."],[10748,"Do the same for