rt."],[8975,"Each stage starts a `workers.train` subprocess (except `clean`, which calls separation's `run_files()` and writes each speaker's primary stem to `dataset_clean/<speaker id>/`). Separate processes have the same rationale as the original: cancellation kills the process tree, CUDA contexts stay clean, and DDP needs its own processes anyway. Worker `metric` events become `train_metrics` (sent to the Web UI's Pinia store for loss curves); full metrics are in the experiment's `metrics.jsonl`, read by `metrics(name, since)`."],[11170,"Each voice has a default preset, created on import from the default parameters in settings. Selecting the voice on another page automatically loads these parameters. Adjust them here and click **Save**. See Voice parameters for their meanings."],[8840,"Each voice has at most one index per speaker key: `default` or `spk<N>`, with filenames `model.index` and `spkid<N>.index`; attaching another replaces the old one (multiple indexes per key are unsupported, decided during import planning). `index_for(voice, speaker_id)` tries `spk<N>`, then `default`; a multi-speaker voice without the appropriate key does not fall back to another speaker's index."],[10454,"Each voice shows its sample rate, version (v1/v2), **pitch guidance** or **no pitch guidance**, and speaker count for multi-speaker voices;"],[11333,"Each voice's default preset"],[10416,"Earlier results"],[11160,"Edit **Name**, **Description** and **Tags** (separated by commas). For voices with several speakers, you can also name each **Speaker N**. Click **Save** when finished."],[8545,"Effect"],[9370,"Effect"],[7437,"Effective settings are merged from four layers, with later layers overriding earlier ones:"],[10424,"Effects"],[10871,"Effects"],[7777,"Effects of `compute.device`, `compute.precision`, `compute.cuda_graph_live`, and `live.enable_asio` on live voice conversion"],[7370,"Effects over the converted voice, as `convert --effect`; replaces the saved chain, `none` clears 