ne"],[10278,"Engine"],[9735,"Engine has no UI dependencies"],[9734,"Engine returns Gradio update dictionaries and Chinese statuses"],[8663,"Engine runtime, GPU lease, GPU memory release"],[10260,"English"],[11308,"Enter a **New voice name** and click **Merge**."],[11312,"Enter a **New voice name**."],[12084,"Enter a **Voice name**, defaulting to the experiment name."],[11544,"Enter a name in **Preset name**."],[11910,"Enter a path in **Dataset folder**, or click **Browse…** to select one."],[11714,"Enter a sufficiently long random string in **Access token**."],[11897,"Enter an **Experiment name**."],[11262,"Enter the original's root directory in **RVC folder** (it should contain an `assets` folder), or click **Browse…** to select it."],[11904,"Enter the path in **Original experiment folder (logs/\\<name>)**. Optionally enter a new **Experiment name** (defaults to the folder name)."],[9033,"Entire `Job`"],[8199,"Entry point"],[9649,"Entry point"],[9532,"Entry points"],[7269,"Enumerate devices again"],[9123,"Enumeration and grouping (`devices.py`)"],[10007,"Environment"],[9918,"Environment variable"],[7424,"Environment variables"],[7442,"Environment variables and overrides apply only in memory and **are not written back** to `settings.toml`. Folder settings overridden by environment variables are marked **Set by an environment variable** in the Web UI, and those pinned by a host program **Set by the application rvc-next runs in**. When `rvc-next config set` changes an overridden setting, it reports \"An environment variable overrides this setting.\"."],[8305,"Environment variables use `__` to separate levels, for example `RVC_NEXT_SERVER__PORT=8000`, `RVC_NEXT_COMPUTE__DEVICE=cpu`; values are parsed as JSON if possible, otherwise as strings, with `null` / `none` meaning empty. Environment variables and overrides are never written back to the file. `RVC_NEXT_DATA_DIR` is not a setting: it determines the data directory itself."],[7657,"Epochs, `[1, 10000]`"],[11020,"Equal to the crossfade"],[9995,"Error shapes, Host / Origin / token, raw uploads, Range, peaks, browse roots, submitting conversion through the API, events listed in OpenAPI"],[8109,"Errors and exit codes"],[8517,"Errors and exit codes"],[10543,"Errors appear where they occur (in the action bar, a job card or a dialog). The title is the translated error type (for example, “A required model file is not installed” or “The GPU is not available or ran out of memory”), followed by the server's specific message (in English). When more information is available, a **Details** button opens the full content, which you can include in a problem report."],[7921,"Errors are defined in `core/errors.py`; `api/errors.py` only maps them. HTTP status codes and CLI exit codes come from the same exception class (see Architecture for the full table). `ERROR_RESPONSES` declares the `ErrorResponse` model for 400/403/404/409, so the generated client knows the error body shape. A few API-specific conventions:"],[10539,"Errors from this page;"],[8300,"Errors reach this table from three sources:"],[7923,"Errors written directly by `SecurityMiddleware` (`bad_host` 400, `bad_origin` 403, `auth_required` 401) bypass exception handlers but have the same shape."],[10611,"esc closes the topmost dialog, menu or sheet (one layer at a time)."],[4476,"esc 关闭最上层的对话框、菜单或侧边栏（一次只关一层）。"],[11053,"Estimated latency ≈ block length + crossfade + 10 ms (alignment search) + block length (output prefill) + the device's input and output latency. Split streams add another block length; input noise reduction adds min(crossfade, 40 ms). The default settings (250 ms block length, 50 ms crossfade) give about 560 ms plus device latency with a duplex stream."],[11943,"Even out each piece (default) / Even out each file / Leave as recorded"],[8010,"Event"],[9029,"Event"],[8009,"Event classes are defined in `core/events/models.py`; all inherit `EventBase` and set `__event_name__`. `EventBase.get_events()` recursively collects all named subclasses."],[8082,"Event schemas use serialization mode, but event fields with defaults may still be optional in TypeScript; comments in `api/types.ts` record this (the server always sends them)."],[8111,"Events"],[8636,"Events"],[7879,"Events and payloads"],[8233,"Events are JSON lines prefixed with `@rvc ` (`protocol/jsonl.py`), with types in `protocol/messages.py`: `progress`, `step`, `log`, `metric`, `output`, `result`, `error`. Lines without the prefix are always treated as `info` logs."],[9503,"Events are JSON lines prefixed with `@rvc ` (`protocol/jsonl.py`); `parse_line()` treats unprefixed lines as info logs. Types are in `protocol/messages.py`: `progress`, `step`, `log`, `metric`, `output`, `result`, `error`."],[8767,"Events carry the full `Job` snapshot, so cannot be sent per audio block"],[7880,"Events in OpenAPI"],[8776,"Events only signal new logs; full contents use REST"],[8769,"Every 2 seconds (`DB_PROGRESS_INTERVAL`)"],[11168,"Every attachment checks that the index fits the voice. Empty indexes with no vectors (the original's `trained_*.index`) and indexes with a mismatched version (256 dimensions for v1, 768 for v2) are rejected."],[8001,"Every client that passes the middleware may name paths on the server (browsing, resolving audio paths, importing models or indexes by path, creating experiments or updating datasets, importing legacy experiments, adding legacy RVC installations, and so on). Only `reveal` requires a local client: a remote browser has no reason to open the file manager on the server's desktop."],[7851,"Every command level accepts `--debug` to enable debug logs:"],[8566,"Every command that lists or displays data has `--json`. `print_json()` serializes `Record` with `model_dump(mode=\"json\")` (recursively handling lists and dictionaries, converting `Path` to strings), so output exactly matches API JSON. This is more than a convention: commands and routes call the same core method and return the same `Record`. `test_model_json_matches_api_shape` directly compares `rvc-next model list --json` with `GET /api/v1/models`."],[8453,"Every file exists with the correct size, with no recorded verification failures"],[8398,"Every file RVC Next uses, organized by category, plus demo voices and `manifest.json`"],[8718,"Every lengthy operation is a job (`core/jobs/`): one card, one cancel button, one log, consistently across the Web UI, API and CLI. This replaces the original's separate progress displays in each tab and global `TRAIN_TASK` lock."],[8797,"Every model type under `models/` (`paths.models_dir`, inside the data directory by default) is a folder with a JSON sidecar:"],[11697,"Every setting can be overridden by an environment variable in the form `RVC_NEXT_<GROUP>__<FIELD>`, for example `RVC_NEXT_SERVER__PORT=8000` or `RVC_NEXT_PATHS__ASSETS_DIR=D:\\rvc-assets`. Environment variables take precedence over `settings.toml`. The UI shows the effective value; edits in the UI write to `settings.toml`, but the environment variable's value stays effective while it is set. Folders pinned by environment variables in **Storage** are marked **Set by an environment variable**. See Configuration and environment variables for the full list, or run `rvc-next env`."],[6417,"Every slice except the last loses its tail (a regression in the original)"],[9584,"Every slice's tail was silently dropped from the original training dataset"],[11535,"Every voice has a **default preset**, created automatically on import and named `Default`, with initial values from `convert.default_params` in settings (the defaults in the table above)."],[9638,"Evidence"],[9854,"Exact pin: the separation adapter was written for this version's `MSSeparator`"],[8244,"Exception"],[9505,"Exception mapping: `Cancelled` → 130; `MissingAssetError` → `asset_missing` (with `detail.assets`); `ModelFormatError` → `invalid_model`; OOM → `compute_unavailable` (`detail.reason = \"out_of_memory\"`); other errors → `internal_error`, first sending the