 name. If pairing is uncertain, the command prints the import plan and exits with code 3. Specify pairs with `--pair voice.pth=index.index` (add `:spkN` for multiple speakers), or use `--keep-unassigned` to put indexes in the unassigned list and assign them later with `rvc-next model index assign`. Training checkpoints (G) are imported as base models by default; add `--extract` to extract a voice instead."],[8358,"Files in the asset directory"],[10437,"Files upload to the server, with upload progress beneath each file. Once uploaded, a play button appears on the left and the duration on the right. Failed uploads show “Could not upload …” and the reason."],[9709,"Fine-tuning"],[8938,"Fingerprint inputs"],[9129,"Fingerprints"],[8957,"Fingerprints (`engine/train/fingerprint.py:of_paths`) are SHA-1 hashes of each filename, size and mtime under the path, plus settings determining output; missing paths and empty folders hash differently. A completed stage records its fingerprint in `StageState.fingerprint`. A path inside the experiment's folder is named relative to it (`base`), so moving the experiments folder or the data directory leaves every stage current; `experiment.json` keeps a dataset folder inside the experiment (`dataset_upload/`) relative too, and records `\"fingerprints\": 2`. An experiment written before (no `fingerprints`) is upgraded when loaded: each stored fingerprint is recomputed the old way, naming paths absolute, as they are now and at the experiment's earlier place (from `data_dir_previous`, or an uploaded dataset's recorded folder); a match gets the new form, anything else keeps its old fingerprint and shows as changed. The index's own `index_fingerprint.json` is carried over the same way when its folder has not moved."],[6216,"First check whether the GPU is actually being used: the \"Selected\" line in `rvc-next doctor` shows the selected device. Common reasons for seeing CPU:"],[6635,"First port to try, `[0, 65535]`; `0` lets the system pick any p