e corresponding service's `require()` call (e.g. `ConversionService.required_assets()`, `LiveService._require_assets()`, `TrainingService._preflight()`); the UI automatically offers downloads through `AssetGate`."],[10542,"If a model needed for the current operation has not been downloaded, the run button in the action bar is replaced by a notice such as “**Needs HuBERT, RMVPE**” and a **Download (353 MB)** button. Clicking shows download progress in place; the run button returns automatically when the download finishes. You do not need to remember which files each feature requires beforehand."],[6481,"If a port is in use (or reserved by the system), the server tries subsequent ports in order, up to 20, and reports \"Port 7868 is unavailable. Using port 7869.\" in the log. With `strict_port` enabled, it exits immediately with code 3. In the Web UI, these settings are **Server address** and **Port** under **Settings** › **General**. After changing them: **Takes effect the next time the server starts.**"],[6849,"If an environment variable overrides the same setting, the command reports \"An environment variable overrides this setting.\"."],[6406,"If an import contains only one compatible voice, pairing is automatic. With multiple voices, scores use experiment names, name similarity, and whether files share a folder. If the match is uncertain, you choose (the Web UI opens **Review the import**; the command line prints the plan and exits with code 3)."],[6229,"If an imported index cannot be paired with certainty (for example, several voices of the same version are imported together and their names do not match), the Web UI opens **Review the import**. Each index lists only version-compatible voices for you to choose. You can also select **Keep unassigned** and assign it later under **Unassigned indexes** in **Models** › **Voices**. The command line prints the import plan and exits with code 3; rerun with `--pair voice.pth=index.index` or `--keep-unassigned`."],[6928,"If an index's pairing is uncertain or a separation checkpoint lacks its configuration, the command prints file and index tables (including compatible voices), then exits with code 3 without importing any files. Given the root directory of an RVC installation, it copies `assets/weights/*.pth` and `added_*.index` files under `assets/indices` and `logs`."],[11203,"If anything is uncertain, **Review the import** opens for you to confirm before importing."],[10766,"If BlackHole does not appear, restart Core Audio with `sudo killall -9 coreaudiod`, or restart the Mac."],[6220,"If CPU is your only option, switch the pitch method to **pm (fast)** and use **Preview 15 s** to tune parameters before converting the whole song. Vocal separation is especially slow on CPU, so skip it if you can."],[11202,"If every file's destination is clear, import finishes immediately with a notification such as **Imported \\{names} with 1 index(es)**."],[10971,"If exclusive mode is on, a **Turn off exclusive mode** button appears; otherwise, **Choose another** is suggested"],[10977,"If exclusive mode is on, a **Turn off exclusive mode** button appears; otherwise, **Choose another** is suggested (another driver of the same device usually works)"],[11098,"If GPU memory runs out, the session stops with **The GPU is not available or ran out of memory**. Both the live process and server automatically unload their loaded models. Close other programs using GPU memory and retry, or switch to CPU in **Settings › Compute**."],[6249,"If memory is still insufficient, set **GPU jobs at once** to 1, reduce the training batch size, disable **Cache the dataset in GPU memory**, or set **Precision** to fp16 (if the GPU supports it)."],[10961,"If no burst comes back, the panel says so: check the connection and raise the levels. If the bursts come back at different times (dropouts, a drifting clock between two devices), try a longer block or devices on one driver. With speakers and a microphone the measurement includes the sound's travel through the air (about 3 ms per metre)."],[6308,"If several GPUs qualify, the one with the highest compute capability is selected; ties are resolved by the largest memory size. `rvc-next doctor` and the device list under **Settings** › **Compute** show each device, the precision assigned by the rules, and the reason (e.g. \"Pascal SM 6.1 and GTX 16xx cards run in fp32\")."],[11479,"If sibilants or breaths have tearing or electronic artifacts, lower it to 0.2–0.3;"],[10386,"If the **Voices** tab shows “No voices yet”, its **Get the demo voices** button also takes you here."],[11597,"If the action bar shows “**Needs Separation: …**”, click **Download** first to get the preset's required separation models."],[8098,"If the CLI needs the same operation, call the same core method (see CLI implementation)."],[7863,"If the dataset needs accompaniment and reverb removed first, use `--clean vocals-clean` to separate before slicing."],[11255,"If the library has no voice of the same version, a message such as **No v1 voice in the library yet** appears."],[11060,"If the live process itself stops (a crash in a driver or GPU library, the system running out of memory), the title is **A background process stopped unexpectedly**, and the message says how it ended (its exit code or signal) and, when its output shows it, why."],[6658,"If the port is in use, subsequent ports are tried in order (up to 20), and the actual port is reported in the log. If all attempts fail, the command exits with code 3. Binding to a non-local address logs a warning and needs no access token (see Remote access and security). After a successful start, stdout prints one line: `SERVER_READY url=http://...`."],[12097,"If the result needs improvement, increase **Epochs** and **Run all** again. Training resumes from the previous checkpoint."],[11446,"If the selected method's model is not downloaded, the run button is replaced by “**Needs RMVPE**” (or the method's other model) and a **Download** button."],[11474,"If the voice has no attached index, this slider is dimmed and shows “This voice has no index, so index strength has no effect. Attach one in Models.” See Model management for attaching indexes. Multi-speaker voices can have a separate index for each speaker; conversion uses the selected speaker's index."],[10456,"If the voice library is empty, this shows “No voices yet” and an **Open Models** button. See Model management for importing and downloading voices."],[10294,"If you are new to the code, read Development environment → Architecture → the layer relevant to your work."],[6525,"If you call the API from another page or tool (such as your own frontend), add its origin to `server.allowed_origins`. The server also enables CORS for these origins (CORS is configured at startup, so changes require a restart):"],[6223,"If you have a training experiment, click **Build from experiment**;"],[11902,"If you have already trained in the original RVC (experiments are under its `logs/<name>`), you can import the experiment and keep using it:"],[6210,"If you have original RVC, point `paths.assets_dir` to its `assets` folder to avoid downloading again; see Migrate from original RVC."],[10342,"If you set `--host` to a non-local address such as `0.0.0.0`, other devices on the local network can access the server without an access token. Anyone who can connect can use every feature, so do this only on a trusted network or add protection of your own, such as a firewall or a VPN; you can also set an optional access token with `rvc-next config set server.access_token <secret>`. See Remote access and security."],[11260,"If you still have the original RVC, you can use its voices directly without copying models. The **Original RVC installs** section at the bottom of **Voices** says: **Voices in an RVC install are used in place; Import all copies them into the library.**"],[11090,"If you unplug headphones or a USB microphone while running:"],[11925,"If your data already follows the original's `Name_ID_Repeat` subfolder convention (for example, `alice_0_1`, `bob_1_2`), click **Fill from Name_ID_Repeat folders** and select their parent folder to fill the table automatically. Each subfolder must follow this format, have an ID from 0–109 and a repeat count of at least 1, map each ID to only one name, and contain audio."],[11593,"If your goal is “separate vocals → convert → add accompaniment back”, you do not need to start here: enable **Separate first** and **Add accompaniment back** on **Convert** to do it in one operation; see Convert › Optional steps. Use this page when you need to **keep** the separated stems, or inspect or process them first."],[11031,"Immediate"],[11036,"Immediate"],[11041,"Immediate"],[11046,"Immediate"],[11051,"Immediate"],[7768,"Immediately"],[7776,"Immediately"],[11575,"Immediately"],[11579,"Immediately"],[7772,"Immediately; changes in the Web UI rescan the voice library"],[7898,"Implementation"],[9252,"Implementation"],[12126,"Import a downloaded model"],[11879,"Import an original RVC experiment"],[12157,"Import and organize voices and indexes; download demo voices, base models, separation models and required assets."],[8752,"Import is not a job: committing an import is synchronous (see “Import sessions” below)."],[7807,"Import models"],[11119,"Import models"],[6909,"Import models. Each file is identified by content; pairing indexes with voices does not depend on file names."],[8182,"Import sessions"],[8613,"Import sessions"],[8687,"Import sessions"],[11121,"Import steps"],[6404,"Import voices if you want them to be independent of the original installation (for example, if you plan to delete it). Each file is identified by content during import; `.pth` and `.index` file names do not need to match:"],[8831,"Import, download, merge, extraction, training export"],[11189,"Imported as a base model by default; you can also choose **Extract a voice**"],[8355,"Imported into the voice library after download, rather than stored in the asset directory"],[8188,"Imported separation models"],[11587,"Imported separation models"],[8932,"Imported separation models (`SeparationLibrary`) are loaded once with the separation worker's `check` action before entering the library (`_check_loads()`, 600-second timeout); mismatched YAML and checkpoints fail at import (`detail.reason = \"separation_load\"`), rather than first use. Stem labels allow only letters, digits, `-`, `_`, and the two must differ. User-defined separation chains are not yet supported."],[8695,"Imported vocal separation models"],[8898,"Imported: `models/base/<slug>/G.pth` (plus optional `D.pth`) and `base.json`. Sample rate, version and pitch guidance are read from G's weights; users fill in nothing. Missing D is allowed (the discriminator trains from scratch, also allowed by the original)."],[10883,"In **Audio devices**, select **Input** (microphone) and **Output** (headphones, or a virtual audio device to use the voice in Discord, OBS and other programs: see Use Live in other apps). Speak into the microphone: the **Input level** meter should move. Click **Test** beside **Output**; you should hear a tone."],[11311,"In **Checkpoint (G\\_\\*.pth path or \\<experiment>/\\<file>)**, enter the checkpoint's full server path, or use `experiment-name/G_xxx.pth` to refer to a checkpoint in an experiment."],[11345,"In **Convert** and voice details: “Changes apply to the next conversion.”, meaning you need to click **Preview 15 s** or **Convert** again after editing;"],[10392,"In **Inputs**, drag an audio file onto “Drop audio files here”, or click it to choose a file. WAV, FLAC, MP3, M4A, OGG and other formats are supported. The file uploads to the server; once uploaded, click the play button on the left to listen."],[11346,"In **Live**: “Changes apply as you drag.”; see Parameters in live voice conversion below."],[12093,"In **Settings**, check the sample rate (40k is usually enough), version v2 and pitch guidance (required for singing)."],[10023,"In `site/`, `bun install --frozen-lockfile`, `bun run check`, `test`, `build`"],[10268,"In a conflict"],[11465,"In cross-gender conversion, if the voice still does not sound right after adjusting **Pitch**, shift **Formant** slightly in the same direction, such as +0.5 to +1 for male-to-female conversion;"],[9651,"In rvc-next"],[7462,"In the \"Type\" column, `str?` and `int?` mean the value can be empty (`null`). An empty folder setting means \"use the default folder under the data directory\"; a relative folder is inside the data directory as well (`results` is `<data directory>/results`, whatever folder rvc-next is started from)."],[10379,"In the **Conversion** group, click **Download everything for Conversion**, or click **Download** on the individual HuBERT and RMVPE rows."],[11662,"In the **Separation** group under **Models › Assets**, click **Download everything for Separation** to download them all at once."],[6397,"In the Web UI: at the bottom of **Models** › **Voices**, find **Original RVC installs**, click **Add an RVC install**, and choose the RVC root directory (it must contain an `assets` folder). Then:"],[8743,"In-process"],[8751,"In-process"],[8747,"In-process (httpx)"],[8155,"In-process publish / subscribe"],[8651,"In-process publish/subscribe"],[8727,"In-process; starts a separation worker first if separation is a preliminary step"],[6893,"Include hidden legacy voices"],[9229,"Including modification time in the key makes overwriting a file (re-exporting, rebuilding an index) take effect automatically, without notifying the runtime. All methods share an `RLock` and can be called from multiple threads."],[9726,"Inconsistent F0 options"],[9728,"Inconsistent training/inference normalization"],[11862,"Increases contrast between text and background"],[8466,"Index"],[8860,"Index"],[11184,"Index `.index`"],[6692,"Index for a `.pth` voice given by path"],[8618,"Index inbox"],[6425,"Index loading"],[11233,"Index pairing states:"],[6422,"Inde