nput and output may then run on different drivers, as **split streams** (one block more latency). To keep one duplex stream, choose the same driver for both under **Advanced**."],[11029,"Input below this level is muted; −60 dB disables it"],[7693,"Input device"],[7307,"Input device ID, name, or `default`"],[7361,"Input gate in dB, `[-60, 0]`; -60 turns it off"],[7729,"Input gate, `[-60, 0]` dB; -60 turns it off"],[7373,"Input level in dB, `[-24, 24]`"],[8632,"Input meter while idle"],[10861,"Input, output and monitor"],[10185,"Input/output levels, load bar (inference time / block length; above 0.8, use warning color and suggest a longer block), latency, underrun and overrun counts"],[9513,"Inputs, preset, resolved models, output directory and format, device and precision; or `{\"action\": \"check\", \"model\": …}`"],[10620,"Install"],[10625,"Install"],[10634,"Install"],[10017,"Install `libportaudio2`, CPU torch, and development dependencies; `pytest -q`"],[10929,"Install a loopback driver such as BlackHole, send the sound to it, and choose its input (an ordinary input device)"],[10761,"Install BlackHole 2ch, either:"],[6624,"Install completion for the current shell"],[6330,"Install DirectML support: `pip install \"rvc-next[directml]\"` (installs `torch-directml` and `onnxruntime-directml`)."],[12169,"Install from source"],[10011,"Install only the latest `ruff`; `ruff check` and `ruff format --check`. Also runs on pull requests"],[6267,"Install the appropriate PyTorch"],[9756,"Install torch first for the same reason as in a user installation: `pyproject.toml` declares only `torch>=2.7.1`, without specifying a build variant. Install the build for your hardware from the PyTorch index first; the subsequent `pip install` sees that the constraint is satisfied and will not fetch another build from PyPI (usually a large CUDA package)."],[9767,"Installation"],[12163,"Installation"],[6193,"Installation and startup"],[12259,"Installation, first run and first conversion"],[12268,"Installation: prepare an isolated Python environment, install PyTorch for your hardware, then install RVC Next."],[1337,"int"],[1413,"int"],[1417,"int"],[1454,"int"],[1520,"int"],[1524,"int"],[1580,"int"],[1584,"int"],[1588,"int"],[7472,"int"],[7548,"int"],[7552,"int"],[7589,"int"],[7655,"int"],[7659,"int"],[7715,"int"],[7719,"int"],[7723,"int"],[1528,"int?"],[1540,"int?"],[7663,"int?"],[7675,"int?"],[6291,"Intel GPU N (Arc, Data Center GPU, recent integrated graphics) on an XPU build of torch. Same fallbacks as `cuda:N`"],[9529,"Intentional behavior changes"],[10511,"Interface overview"],[10470,"Intermediate separated stems are deleted after conversion. If you also need these stems, use the Vocal separation page first, then send the vocals to Convert."],[10036,"Internationalization"],[7849,"Interrupted with ctrl+c, or the job was cancelled"],[7836,"Invalid input (`invalid_input`, `invalid_path`, `invalid_model`)"],[8045,"Invalidate experiment lists, details, and checkpoints"],[8029,"Invalidate output lists"],[8037,"Invalidate preset queries"],[8069,"Invalidate settings and `meta`"],[8033,"Invalidate voice lists, separation presets, and corresponding details"],[8093,"InvokeAI probes a port with `connect`, then lets uvicorn bind after services load. Probing only detects listening ports; Windows reserved port ranges, where nothing listens but binding is impossible, can appear free. The entire startup interval between probing and binding also lets another process take the port. Binding directly is the only reliable answer, and passing that exact socket to uvicorn removes the gap. The `SERVER_READY` line and `server.json` let launchers, scripts, and other programs discover port changes—log warnings are not machine-readable. `--strict-port` is for deployments with fixed port mappings (reverse proxies, containers), where silently changing ports would conceal the problem."],[1958,"InvokeAI 先 `connect` 探测端口，再在服务加载完后让 uvicorn 绑定。探测只能发现“有人在监听”的端口，Windows 的保留端口段这类“没人监听但绑不上”的情况会被误判为空闲；探测和绑定之间还有一整段启动时间，别的进程可以抢占。直接绑定是唯一可靠的答案，而把测试过的套接字原样交给 uvicorn，就不存在空档。`SERVER_READY` 一行和 `server.json` 则让启动器、脚本和其他程序得知端口变化——日志里的警告对机器不可读。`--strict-port` 用于端口映射固定的部署（反向代理、容器），那里悄悄换端口只会掩盖问题。"],[9742,"Isolated virtual environment"],[12177,"Isolated virtual environment"],[10275,"Isolated virtual environment, dependency constraints and their reasons, every `scripts/dev.py` task, building the wheel and documentation site"],[9716,"Issue"],[9535,"Issues found in the original and their resolution"],[10269,"It and the code take precedence"],[8226,"It owns the audio devices and real-time threads, which need isolation from the server's event loop, GIL contention and possible crashes"],[9929,"It runs the original `infer.vc.pipeline.Pipeline` and RVC Next on CPU, fp32, with the same seed and 16 kHz input, printing one line per case; any case exceeding the tolerance (RMS per-sample difference on a -1..1 scale, `1e-4`) causes exit code 1. See Parity with the original for case design and which results are bit-identical."],[9890,"It runs these five steps in order, stopping at the first failure. CI runs the same checks (see “CI” below):"],[6326,"It works only on NVIDIA CUDA: on ROCm and XPU the switches have no effect and inference runs normally. Recordings are cached by input shape (up to 8 per call site, adjustable with `RVC_NEXT_CUDA_GRAPH_MAX_CACHE`). If recording fails, inference automatically falls back to normal mode. Offline inputs vary in length, making recordings hard to reuse, so it is disabled by default."],[10574,"Item"],[10897,"Item"],[10936,"Item"],[11063,"Item"],[10573,"Items in the **More actions** menu:"],[10006,"Job"],[10519,"Job cards"],[10545,"Job cards appear in the action bar of the page that started them and in the **Jobs** sheet. Each card shows:"],[9085,"Job history and retry"],[7403,"Job ID (required)"],[8167,"Job queue, resources, runners, history"],[8241,"Job requests are stored as JSON in the database. Factories registered by `kind` reconstruct `