ophone without complaint. With **Driver** on **Auto**, rvc-next does this switch itself: it opens the device through the recommended driver, and when that one refuses, tries the device's other drivers one by one (in the order of preference above) until one opens it. This applies to Start, the input meter, **Hear yourself**, **Test** and the check before Start."],[6259,"Once a token is set, all browsers (including those on the server machine) require it, so a forgotten token can only be reset from the command line. The browser shows the **Access token** dialog; enter the new token."],[6491,"Once a token is set, every request under `/api/`, `/ws/`, `/openapi.json`, and `/docs` must carry it, using any of these three methods:"],[6488,"Once it is set, an **Access token** dialog appears when the page loads (\"This server asks for its access token.\"). Enter the token and click **Save**. The browser saves the token in local storage and writes a Cookie named `rvc_next_token` (for audio playback and WebSocket connections), so you do not need to enter it again next time. If the token is incorrect or changes, the dialog reappears."],[10492,"Once satisfied, click **Convert**."],[10343,"Once the page opens, you will see the navigation bar on the left (at the bottom in narrow windows): **Convert**, **Live**, **Separate**, **Train**, **Models**, and **Settings** at the bottom. The first visit opens **Convert**; subsequent visits return to the page you last used. See Interface overview for explanations of each part of the interface."],[10325,"Once the server starts, the terminal prints a line like:"],[6393,"Once you point to the original `assets` folder, assets downloaded later in RVC Next (such as FCPE or missing base models) are also written there."],[8219,"One `workers.separate` subprocess per job"],[8222,"One `workers.train` subprocess per stage"],[8735,"One `workers.train` subprocess per stage"],[8775,"One batch every 0.25 seconds, at most 50 lines (`MAX_LOG_EVENT_LINES`)"],[