n the output opened through WASAPI (or will: the first driver to try). Exclusive mode can reduce latency, but prevents other programs from using the device at the same time. Turning it on fixes the output's driver to WASAPI: an exclusive stream that fails is reported, not replaced by a shared one through another driver."],[11044,"Shown while either noise reduction is on: how much quieter the noise gets; 1 removes the most and can take some voice with it"],[10224,"Shrinkable names, one column of sections + `PageFooter`, centered field rows, no grids placing sections side by side"],[8800,"Sidecar"],[10261,"Simplified Chinese"],[9954,"Simulates both `added_*` and `trained_*` indexes for content identification tests (width 256 / 768, `ntotal == 0`)"],[12199,"Since PyTorch is already installed, pip considers the `torch` dependency satisfied and will not replace it with another build. After installation, the `rvc-next` command is available in the environment."],[9218,"Single entry"],[9489,"Single GPU or CPU in-process; multiple GPUs use DDP over gloo, one spawn process per card"],[6443,"Single-speaker slicing also processes only top-level audio files in the dataset folder (matching dataset scanning). A voice is considered multi-speaker based on speaker information in the `.pth`, rather than the number of embedding rows (every trained voice has 109 rows)."],[11533,"Single-speaker voices do not show this dropdown and use ID 0. Speaker names can be edited in voice details; see Model management. Specify one on the command line with `--speaker <id>`."],[11450,"Situation"],[9382,"Skip the voice and return (gated, denoised) input, replacing the original's `im` mode"],[6423,"Skipped whenever `added_*.index` exists"],[12037,"Slice"],[12041,"Slice"],[7213,"Slice length, `[0.5, 10]`; saved"],[9477,"slicer2 (−42 dB), about 3.7 s per slice with 0.3 s overlap, causal high-pass then normalisation before writing; **every slice's tail is written** (fixing an original regression); complete