) do not use pitch. This row is dimmed, the selected method has no effect, and no pitch model download is required."],[11481,"Voices with **no pitch guidance** do not use this parameter; the slider is dimmed and shows “This voice has no pitch guidance, so this has no effect.” With **Frames without pitch** set to **Fill in (RVC 2026)** it has no effect either, and the slider says so."],[11259,"Voices with Applio's **RefineGAN** or **MRF HiFi-GAN** vocoders, and voices trained on a custom content-feature model, cannot be used: importing one says why, and it is skipped."],[11257,"Voices with Applio's default vocoder (HiFi-GAN) are RVC voices and work as they are. Their author, epoch, step and training length appear in **About**; a multi-speaker voice gets numbered speakers you can rename."],[11004,"Voices with several speakers show a **Speaker** menu that can also be changed while running. Changing voices resets the speaker to the new voice's first speaker. If that speaker has a dedicated index (`spk<N>`), it switches to that index as well."],[11164,"Voices with several speakers show an **Index** dropdown to select whether the next attached index is `default` or a speaker-specific index."],[10455,"Voices without an index have a **no index** label; voices from an original RVC installation (read directly, without copying into the library) have a **legacy** label."],[10285,"Vue 3 frontend: directory structure, `ui/` components and MD3 motion, unified experience contract, data flow, layout rules, internationalisation, tests and adding a page"],[4150,"Vue 3 前端：目录结构、`ui/` 组件与 MD3 动效、统一体验约定、数据流、布局规则、国际化、测试、如何新增页面"],[10045,"Vue 3.5, `<script setup lang=\"ts\">`"],[3910,"Vue 3.5、`<script setup lang=\"ts\">`"],[10053,"Vue Router 5, **hash history**"],[3918,"Vue Router 5，**hash 历史**"],[8089,"Warn before binding to a non-loopback address (`server.access_token` is not required)."],[8579,"Warn when the host is not loopback (no access token is required)."],[10922,"WASAPI loopback"],[4787,"WASAPI 环回"],[5692,"WAV"],[11827,"WAV"],[6344,"Ways to reduce GPU memory use:"],[3883,"Web UI"],[3890,"Web UI"],[4149,"Web UI"],[10018,"Web UI"],[10025,"Web UI"],[10284,"Web UI"],[3519,"Web UI + API"],[9654,"Web UI + API"],[9772,"Web UI package manager, build and tests"],[9888,"Web UI tests"],[1391,"Web UI 可以浏览的服务器文件夹。为空时为：用户主目录、各个原版 RVC 安装、数据目录，以及所有驱动器（Windows）或已挂载的卷（macOS 的 `/Volumes/*`，Linux 的 `/media/<用户>/*`、`/run/media/<用户>/*`、`/mnt/*`）"],[3904,"Web UI 是 `rvc_next/webui/` 下的一个 Vue 3 项目，同时也是一个 Python 包：构建产物 `dist/` 被 git 忽略，作为包数据打进 wheel，由 API 的 `SPAStaticFiles` 提供（见 API 与事件）。它没有自己的业务逻辑——REST 是唯一的数据来源，socket 事件只负责让缓存保持新鲜。"],[3891,"Web UI 是 rvcnext/webui/ 下的一个 Vue 3 项目，同时也是一个 Python 包：构建产物 dist/ 被 git 忽略，作为包数据打进 wheel，由 API 的 SPAStaticFiles` 提供（见 API 与事件）。"],[3753,"Web UI 测试"],[3637,"Web UI 的包管理器、构建与测试"],[268,"Web UI 默认允许浏览已添加的原版 RVC 安装中的文件（见 远程访问与安全 中的浏览范围）。"],[379,"Web UI（包括本机浏览器）浏览和使用服务器上的文件时，只能使用 `paths.browse_roots` 中的文件夹，超出范围的路径会被拒绝（`invalid_path`）。默认（列表为空）包括："],[3684,"Web 侧执行 `bun run dev --port <web-port> --strictPort`，并设置 `RVC_NEXT_BACKEND=http://127.0.0.1:<api-port>`。`vite.config.ts` 把 `/api`、`/openapi.json` 和 `/ws` 代理到这个地址（默认 `http://127.0.0.1:7868`），浏览器打开 `http://localhost:<web-port>` 即可。"],[1858,"WebSocket 被拒绝时以关闭码 1008 断开。中间件读取的设置都是函数（`lambda: services.settings.settings.server.access_token`），所以在设置页修改令牌或允许的源立即生效，不必重启。"],[6991,"Weight of the first voice, `[0, 1]`"],[8427,"Weights bundled with torchcrepe 0.0.24 (MIT)"],[8424,"Weights bundled with torchfcpe 0.0.4 (the model RVC uses through `spawn_bundled_infer_model`)"],[10868,"What if the output device is missing?"],[10514,"What is kept when switching pages"],[12134,"What it can do"],[9782,"What it does"],[11485,"What it does"],[11500,"What it does"],[6151,"What it holds"],[9650,"What it is"],[6454,"What remote browsers can do"],[12222,"What RVC Next can do"],[10215,"What they enforce"],[10298,"What was taken"],[12075,"When **Train** starts, if the experiment folder already contains G/D checkpoints, training resumes from the latest pair rather than starting over. Create a new experiment to train entirely from scratch."],[9340,"When `formant == 0`, `n_res` is `None` and the call is exactly the same as the original, so output with default parameters is bit-identical."],[7990,"When `server.access_token` is set, requests under `/api/`, `/ws/`, `/openapi.json`, and `/docs` must carry a token; `/api/v1/app/health` is exempt. Otherwise 401 `auth_required`"],[6173,"When `True`, a taken port is an error"],[7820,"When a command fails, the log prints an error message and the exit code indicates the error category (defined in `rvc_next/core/errors.py`):"],[11316,"When a command-line import encounters uncertain pairings, it prints the plan and exits with code 3. Use `--pair`, `--keep-unassigned` and `--extract` to decide. See Command reference for full details."],[10442,"When a folder is an input, conversion processes all audio files at its **top level**, excluding subfolders."],[10565,"When a job started on another page finishes or fails, a notification appears at the bottom of the screen, such as “… finished”. Failure notifications include an **Open log** button that opens the jobs sheet."],[10148,"When a new navigation interrupts an unfinished transition, finish the old one first; rejected Promises from skipped transitions are all caught."],[6497,"When a token is set, all requests must pass the token check first. The server then (or right away, without a token) determines which operations to allow based on whether the request comes from the local machine:"],[6519,"When allowing other computers to connect, narrow the scope to the folders you need:"],[10517,"When an error occurs"],[6352,"When an experiment's **GPUs** setting is `cpu` (new experiments take the default from `training.gpus`), training also runs as a CPU job."],[10992,"When another driver had to open the device, a note below it says which one, and what the drivers before it said: **Opened through DirectSound, as the drivers before it refused (WASAPI: …)**."],[8937,"When applicable"],[10576,"When available"],[7984,"When bound to loopback, the `Host` header must be `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, `::1`, the bound hostname, or `extra_hosts` (kept by reference, so names added later count at once, which `RvcNextServer.allow_host()` relies on); otherwise 400 `bad_host`"],[10582,"When browser and server are on the same computer"],[10438,"When browser and server are on the same computer (or the server has an access token set), a **Server files** button appears. It uses files directly from the server's disk, **without uploading**, making it suitable for large files or large numbers of files:"],[6514,"When browsing or using server files, the Web UI (including local browsers) can access only folders in `paths.browse_roots`. Paths outside this scope are rejected (`invalid_path`). By default (an empty list), the scope includes:"],[10487,"When buttons are unavailable, the left side explains why: “Choose a voice.” or “Add audio to convert.” You also cannot start while inputs are still uploading. If required models are missing (HuBERT, the selected pitch method's model, separation models), the buttons are replaced by “**Needs …**” and a **Download** button; see Interface overview."],[11559,"When changes apply"],[11777,"When empty (default), this includes your home folder, added original RVC installs, the data folder and every drive (Windows `C:\\`, `D:\\`…) or mounted volume (macOS `/Volumes/…`; Linux `/media/<user>/…`, `/run/media/<user>/…`, `/mnt/…`). The gray placeholder lists the folders currently allowed. Entering paths restricts access to those folders."],[10934,"When enabled while running: with a monitor device, the monitor receives the original audio while the output stays converted; without one, the output switches directly to the original audio (temporarily bypassing conversion)."],[10933,"When enabled while stopped: passes audio through without loading a voice."],[6766,"When finished, prints output file paths one per line."],[6340,"When inference or training reports an out-of-memory error (CUDA `OutOfMemoryError` or the corresponding MPS or DirectML errors):"],[12052,"When it runs"],[7764,"When it takes effect"],[6183,"When listening only locally, the server accepts only requests whose `Host` is a local name or the bound address. A tunnel (such as a Gradio share link) or a reverse proxy forwards its own public host name, which has to be allowed first. A tunnel's address is often known only once the server has started and its port is fixed, so `allow_host()` can be called after `start()` too and takes effect at once:"],[6357,"When live voice conversion stops, waiting jobs start automatically."],[10516,"When models are missing"],[11998,"When off, the trained voice has no pitch guidance (suited to speech rather than singing), and the **Pitch** stage is skipped"],[8248,"When raised"],[8060,"When re-enumeration finds a change"],[10930,"When recording is not possible, the device panel says why. Send the converted voice to a **different** device than the one being recorded (headphones, or a virtual cable for another program): recording the output that plays the voice would feed it back into itself, so rvc-next refuses it (**Records its own output**). Turning the setting off hides these inputs again."],[10149,"When supported, `App.vue` renders views directly without `<Transition>`; otherwise it falls back to `<Transition mode=\"out-in\">` with `fade-through`."],[11551,"When switching **Pitch method**, the new method's model loads in the background. If it has not been downloaded, conversion continues using the previous method and reports the missing model."],[8984,"When switching voices, the worker replies with a `State` containing `voice_path` for **the voice actually converting now**: the new voice, or the old one retained after loading failure. The service looks it up in `_voice_ids` (model path → voice id), making state follow the worker rather than the request, and updates `live.last_voice` to the actual voice in use. A speaker out of range for the new voice resets to 0. F0 method changes check assets first; if the worker cannot load the new method, it keeps the old one."],[10388,"When the download finishes, the row shows **Installed** and an **In library** button; click it to open the voice's details. The voice also appears in **Models › Voices**."],[6187,"When the host program is itself a FastAPI (or any ASGI) application, it can mount RVC Next instead of opening another port:"],[6251,"When the number of GPU jobs reaches **GPU jobs at once**, other jobs queue. While live voice conversion runs, new GPU jobs also wait to avoid affecting live audio. **Run anyway** on the job card starts a job without waiting for live voice conversion to stop (which may cause audio glitches)."],[11093,"When the original device reappears (including under another driver), the stream reopens automatically and returns to **Running**, without reloading the voice."],[6530,"When the server listens only locally, the forwarded `Host` must be `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` (otherwise 400 `bad_host`); a program embedding rvc-next can allow a proxy's or a tunnel's public host name with `extra_hosts` / `allow_host()` (Embedding);"],[10599,"When there is more than one result, **Download all** appears at the top right of the list to download them as a zip."],[9837,"When writing documentation:"],[10999,"When you click **Start**, if the saved **Output** device is missing but the system default is available, rvc-next asks for confirmation before sending audio there (it could be your speakers): **The saved output device is missing; the system default would be used.** It continues only after you click **Start with the default output**. If the input or monitor device cannot be found at all, it reports an error; select another device first."],[10458,"When you select a voice, **Voice parameters** loads that voice's default preset automatically, so the same voice sounds consistent in conversion and live voice conversion. RVC Next remembers the last voice you selected on this page."],[7461,"Whenever a running server reads settings, it checks at most once per second whether another process (`rvc-next config set` or a text editor) has changed `settings.toml`. If so, it reloads the file and notifies open Web UI sessions. When the Web UI saves settings, it also reads the file first, merges with its current contents, and writes it back without overwriting changes made elsewhere. If a manual edit cannot be parsed or fails validation, the server logs a warning and continues using the previous settings."],[10962,"Whenever you change devices, rvc-next actually tries to open them with the current configuration in the background: it checks the settings with the driver and, while Live is stopped, runs the output and monitor for a moment (the input is already open for the **Input level** meter). Problems therefore appear below the relevant device before you click **Start**, and so does a failed **Test** sound or **Hear yourself**. The format is **reason: explanation from the server** (the explanation is supplied by the server in English, naming the device):"],[10428,"Where files are saved and how they are named"],[11789,"Where files come from: **Hugging Face**, **hf-mirror.com**, **ModelScope** or **Custom**"],[8210,"Where it runs"],[11676,"Where settings are saved"],[12104,"Where to start for common tasks"],[12215,"Whether `ffmpeg` is found (optional; PyAV can decode without it);"],[12216,"Whether audio devices are available (required for live voice conversion);"],[11843,"Whether new experiments save a voice at every save point"],[6179,"Whether to open a browser after starting; `False` by default"],[7435,"Which changes require a restart"],[11883,"Which stages must rerun after settings change?"],[11089,"While a session is active (running, loading, reconnecting, etc.), every page's top bar shows a Live chip, for example **Live · 620 ms**. During loading and similar operations, it shows the current state instead. Click the chip to return to **Live**; the button on its right stops the session from any page. The chip turns red on reconnection or error."],[10758,"While a voice chat program records, Windows may lower every other sound. To stop that, open the Sound Control Panel's **Communications** tab and choose **Do nothing**."],[11079,"While Live runs, **Record** beside the start button writes the session to a WAV file in the outputs folder (`<date>/live/`). Choose what to keep:"],[10609,"While live voice conversion is running, a chip appears before the buttons on the right of the top bar, visible on every page. It shows “Live · N ms” (estimated latency) while running, or the current state during startup, loading or reconnection, such as “Loading the voice…” or “Reconnecting the device…”. Click the chip to open **Live**; click the square **Stop** button beside it to stop live voice conversion directly. See Live voice conversion."],[12076,"While running, the **Run** step shows a job card and a progress bar appears below the step bar. The same job appears in the top-bar **Jobs** panel, where you can read its log. Training queues as a GPU job: if live voice conversion is using the GPU, it shows **Waiting for the GPU**. You can click **Run anyway** (which may cause live audio glitches)."],[11754,"While the device panel is shown, it keeps the microphone open and shows **Input level** even when Live is stopped. The microphone is released about 15 seconds after the page is closed or hidden. Turn this off if you do not want the microphone kept in use"],[10911,"While the server is still listing the devices (a moment, longer with many drivers installed), each menu says **Looking for audio devices…**."],[12223,"Who it is for"],[9234,"Who unloads what after OOM is a core policy (`release_after_oom`); see Core services."],[9700,"Why"],[8505,"Why not download directly from distributions: these `.7z` files use solid compression; voices share 1.3–1.9 GB compressed blocks with other assets, so fetching one file requires downloading and decompressing at least its entire block. This is a major reason for rvc-model."],[8412,"Why rvc-model exists: the official repository retains an early flat layout, mixing code, Windows executables, and tens of GB of distributions; some models (demo voices) exist only inside `.7z` distributions and cannot be downloaded individually (see below). rvc-model copies the required files unchanged into categories, making each file available separately."],[8861,"Width `d` (256 → v1, 768 → v2), vector count `ntotal` (0 means `trained_` index), `engine/index/inspect.py`"],[1651,"Windows"],[4212,"Windows"],[4521,"Windows"],[4525,"Windows"],[4786,"Windows"],[7786,"Windows"],[10347,"Windows"],[10656,"Windows"],[10660,"Windows"],[10921,"Windows"],[12189,"Windows and Linux:"],[12191,"Windows and Linux:"],[12193,"Windows and Linux:"],[10743,"Windows lets a program take a device for itself (*exclusive mode*): while it holds the device, no other program can play or record through it. By default every device allows this, and an exclusive request even takes the device away from programs already using it (\"Give exclusive mode applications priority\"). Some games, voice chat programs and audio players ask for exclusive mode, and then rvc-next loses the microphone or the virtual device in the middle of a session (Live goes to **Reconnecting the device…**), or cannot open it at all (**In use by another program**). The other program can lose it to rvc-next the same way."],[9668,"Windows VST2/VST3 plugin (iPlug2) driving a Python worker"],[3533,"Windows VST2/VST3 插件（iPlug2）驱动一个 Python worker"],[4608,"Windows 允许一个程序把设备据为己有（*独占模式*）：它占着设备时，其他程序都不能通过这台设备播放或录音。默认情况下每台设备都允许这样做，而且独占请求甚至会把设备从正在使用它的程序手里抢走（“给与独占模式应用程序优先”）。有些游戏、语音聊天程序和播放器会请求独占模式，这时 rvc-next 会在会话中途失去麦克风或虚拟声卡（实时变声进入 **正在重新连接设备…**），或者根本打不开它（**被其他程序占用**）。反过来，其他程序也可能这样被 rvc-next 抢走设备。"],[6054,"Windows 和 Linux